		{ f="2210-65a396a9", h="65a396a9", t="Word is that Vance Undergloom has taken a permanent room upstairs at the Gallows' End Tavern at the southeast end of town.  I think he's just off the reading room.", d=11.760, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-74086731", h="74086731", t="You aiming to be a taxidermist?  I don't like people who think they can stuff and mount me because they think I'm dead.  No?  Good!  Look for Rand Rhobart at a camp to the southeast of town.  To get to him take the road southeast out of Brill and hang a left at the intersection.", d=18.880, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-7b3b448d", h="7b3b448d", t="I guess your first exercise is going to be to mine your way down to the Undercity.  Heh, get it?  Mine... nevermind.  To get to the Undercity go to the rear of the Ruins of Lordaeron south of Brill, and take the elevator down.  Ask one of the Undercity Guardians there for further assistance.", d=21.680, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-7c3c6d67", h="7c3c6d67", t="Look for Faruza.  Last I saw she was standing out front between the stables and the house on the northwest end of town.", d=8.400, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-86caa6f1", h="86caa6f1", t="Fancy yourself a chef?  Head to the Undercity south of town for your training.  You can catch the elevators heading down at the back of the Ruins of Lordaeron.  Talk to one of those lumbering Undercity Guardians for further assistance once you arrive.", d=15.760, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-887305c0", h="887305c0", t="Rupert Boch is his name.  I hear that he's upstairs in one of the rooms at the Gallows' End Tavern on the southeast end of town.", d=8.720, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-8a371927", h="8a371927", t="Now if I were Innkeeper Renee where might I be?  Hmmm?  Oh, perhaps inside the Gallows' End Tavern.  Yes, that's it, I'm sure of it.  Try the southeast end of Brill... think you can find that?", d=14.080, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-8a7ec9f6", h="8a7ec9f6", t="It is Bowen Brisboise that you seek then.  You'll find him inside his house southwest of Brill just on the other side of the bridge at Cold Hearth Manor.", d=10.200, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-9194163f", h="9194163f", t="Ah, you seek Dark Cleric Beryl.  He's upstairs in the reading room at the Gallows' End Tavern.  Reading, praying, who knows what he's up to, and who would dare to ask?", d=12.640, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-947eed23", h="947eed23", t="Butcher you say?  Oh, First Aid Trainer!  Same thing.  When you see Nurse Neela standing just inside the Gallows' End Tavern on the southeast side of town you'll know why.", d=11.880, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-9a74b5f1", h="9a74b5f1", t="You can find Vance Undergloom upstairs in a room at the Gallows' End Tavern on the southeast side of Brill.", d=8.160, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-a67f19d2", h="a67f19d2", t="Clyde Kellen, the local bass master, has his favorite fishing spot just east of Brill at Brightwater Lake.", d=7.600, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-aa0b50b4", h="aa0b50b4", t="Yeah, you'll always find Clyde Kellen fishing on the bank of Brightwater Lake just east of Brill.  Just watch out for psychos wearing masks while you're out there.  We had to shut down the kids' summer camp last year.", d=11.880, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-aaa369e6", h="aaa369e6", t="Our Alchemist's name is Carolai Anise.  You'll find her in a house at the northwest end of Brill.", d=7.400, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-aab0700b", h="aab0700b", t="Actually I prefer traditional medicines... leeches, maggots, bonesaws... that sort of thing.  Well to each their own.  You can find the our local Herbalism Trainer, Faruza, standing out front near the stables in Brill.", d=15.080, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-bc428669", h="bc428669", t="Morganus the stable master can be found out in front of the stables strangely enough.", d=6.200, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-bff3d364", h="bff3d364", t="That would be Shelene Rhobart.  Take the road southeast out of Brill then head east at the intersection.  She's at a camp along the side of the road.", d=10.520, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-cba2e53b", h="cba2e53b", t="Look inside the Gallows' End Tavern's main dining room for Austil de Mon.  The tavern is on the southeast edge of Brill.", d=7.960, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-d67fe744", h="d67fe744", t="The Rogue Trainer's name is Marion Call.  You can find her upstairs in the reading room at the Gallows' End Tavern at the town's southeast edge.", d=10.840, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-d821d003", h="d821d003", t="Sorry friend, we don't have one of those here in Brill.  You'll have to head to the Undercity for that.  The Undercity is underneath the Ruins of Lordaeron to the south of Brill.  From the back of the ruins take the elevator down and then speak to one of the Undercity Guardians to find your way further.", d=21.440, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-dc5df42b", h="dc5df42b", t="Black, grey and dark purple are the prescribed colors.  See to it that you don't stray onto the wrong side of fashion street friend.  Bowen Brisboise can help to see that you don't.  You'll find him inside Cold Hearth Manor on the other side of the bridge to the southwest of town.", d=21.000, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-ddd22a35", h="ddd22a35", t="That's Rupert Boch you're looking for.  He and his entourage have a room upstairs at the Gallows' End Tavern on the southeast end of Brill.", d=9.160, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-e7cb64ec", h="e7cb64ec", t="There's a Bat Handler inside the Undercity.  Head south down the road out of Brill, then west at the T-intersection.  The Ruins of Lordaeron will be on your left.  Go into them and then down into the Undercity.  You can ask an Undercity Guardian there for further assistance.", d=20.160, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-ef767f20", h="ef767f20", t="Which profession?", d=1.680, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-effe3a80", h="effe3a80", t="What could you possibly need a bank for?  Very well, you'll need to go through the Ruins of Lordaeron to the south of Brill.  In the back are a set of elevators leading down into the Undercity.  When you get there stop any of those lumbering Abominations they like to call an Undercity Guardian and ask it for better directions.", d=22.870, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
		{ f="2210-f7d8157b", h="f7d8157b", t="Marion Call is keeping Dark Cleric Beryl company in the reading room upstairs at the Gallows' End Tavern on the southeast edge of Brill.  I'm just dying to see who wins that staring contest.", d=13.200, v="scourge-female-warrior" },
	},
	[2215] = {
		{ f="2215-dc484bb4", h="dc484bb4", t="In order to serve the Dark Lady and Varimathras we need to advance the front on the Human Infestation.", d=8.760, v="scourge-female-warrior", s={ ["m"]=8.120 } },
	},
	[2216] = {
		{ f="2216-8e0e34da", h="8e0e34da", t="We are but so close to developing the New Plague that our Dark Lady desires with such fervor.", d=6.960, v="scourge-male-dark" },
	},
	[2226] = {
		{ f="2226-dd7de3ae", h="dd7de3ae", t="Greetings.  Our bats are well trained and fed.  You'll not find faster.", d=7.880, v="scourge-male-standard" },
	},
	[2238] = {
		{ f="2238-5408b909", h="5408b909", t="Marlgen... One of the jailors. He has the key to my bonds.", d=6.160, v="orc-male-shady" },
		{ f="2238-6d472bad", h="6d472bad", t="Get away from here, $c, or they'll put you in chains as well.", d=4.440, v="orc-male-shady" },
	},
	[2239] = {
		{ f="2239-4513b5ec", h="4513b5ec", t="Do you mock me while I am unable to defend myself, bound to this ball of iron?", d=7.920, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="2239-7c058ec5", h="7c058ec5", t="One of the humans has the key to this infernal contraption. Eston I think they said his name was.", d=10.720, v="orc-male-guard" },
	},
	[2299] = {
		{ f="2299-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.080, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
	},
	[2302] = {
		{ f="2302-1ce5dd77", h="1ce5dd77", t="Greetings $c.  Do you wish to aid the Silverwing Sentinels in their fight at Warsong Gulch?", d=6.439, v="nightelf-female-sentinel" },
		{ f="2302-7e5b36ab", h="7e5b36ab", t="I am sorry $c, but you are not seasoned enough yet to enter Warsong Gulch.", d=7.603, v="nightelf-female-sentinel" },
	},
	[2310] = {
		{ f="2310-81663044", h="81663044", t="I'm working on delicate matters of Horde intelligence. It would be best for us both if you did not disturb me.", d=10.400, v="scourge-female-standard" },
	},
	[2326] = {
		{ f="2326-33af2c00", h="33af2c00", t="I've heard it said that Deneb Walker, holed up in Stromgarde, has a book that is sure to help improve your First Aid techniques.", d=9.480, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
		{ f="2326-a28d29e1", h="a28d29e1", t="I can train you in First Aid techniques.", d=3.200, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
		{ f="2326-c2e96a28", h="c2e96a28", t="The esteemed Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen can train you further.  He can be found in Theramore treating the wounded at the barracks.", d=8.960, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
	},
	[2327] = {
		{ f="2327-2957a3a0", h="2957a3a0", t="Oh, a fellow Physician. I would be glad to teach you anything that would aid your journeys.", d=6.920, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="2327-33af2c00", h="33af2c00", t="I've heard it said that Deneb Walker, holed up in Stromgarde, has a book that is sure to help improve your First Aid techniques.", d=8.480, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="2327-b55ad3db", h="b55ad3db", t="Yes my $g son : daughter;? What can I assist you with?", d=3.320, v="human-female-official", g=true },
		{ f="2327-c2e96a28", h="c2e96a28", t="The esteemed Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen can train you further.  He can be found in Theramore treating the wounded at the barracks.", d=7.960, v="human-female-official" },
	},
	[2329] = {
		{ f="2329-33af2c00", h="33af2c00", t="I've heard it said that Deneb Walker, holed up in Stromgarde, has a book that is sure to help improve your First Aid techniques.", d=7.600, v="human-female-standard" },
		{ f="2329-a28d29e1", h="a28d29e1", t="I can train you in First Aid techniques.", d=2.360, v="human-female-standard" },
		{ f="2329-c2e96a28", h="c2e96a28", t="The esteemed Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen can train you further.  He can be found in Theramore treating the wounded at the barracks.", d=7.800, v="human-female-standard" },
	},
	[2352] = {
		{ f="2352-03ca5480", h="03ca5480", t="Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.   ", d=28.137, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-174473b0", h="174473b0", t="Recently, a night elf druid named Naralex discovered a network of underground caverns within the heart of the Barrens. Believing he could use the caverns' springs to restore lushness to the Barrens, the druid began siphoning the energies of the fabled Emerald Dream. His vision somehow became a nightmare, however, and soon the Wailing Caverns changed into a den of vicious, deadly predators. It is said that Naralex still resides somewhere inside the labyrinth, trapped beyond the edges of the Emerald Dream.  ", d=36.427, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-17e9d243", h="17e9d243", t="Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world's creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone.  ", d=35.094, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-19490f29", h="19490f29", t="Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar's spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ", d=35.674, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-19cbe7de", h="19cbe7de", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Bolvar, Magni, or Tyrande.", d=18.679, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-1a6e2552", h="1a6e2552", t="This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul'Farrak's walls. ", d=30.037, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-22aa3fe4", h="22aa3fe4", t="Razorfen Downs can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the east side of the road.", d=6.054, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-2e88eda5", h="2e88eda5", t="Frustrated by the Dalaran wizards' lack of progress against the undead during the Third War, the Archmage Arugal elected to summon the extra-dimensional worgen to bolster his side's diminishing ranks. The wolf-men slaughtered the Scourge, then quickly turned on the wizards themselves and laid siege to the keep of the noble, Baron Silverlaine. The fort quickly fell into shadow and ruin. Driven mad with guilt, Arugal adopted the worgen as his children and retreated to the newly dubbed 'Shadowfang Keep'.  ", d=33.783, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-3141b27b", h="3141b27b", t="Crafted from the same vines as Razorfen Kraul, Razorfen Downs is the traditional capital city of the quilboar race. The sprawling, thorn-ridden labyrinth houses a veritable army of loyal quilboar as well as their high priests - the Death's Head tribe. Recently, however, a looming shadow has fallen over the crude den. Agents of the undead Scourge - led by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer - have taken control over the quilboar race and turned the maze of thorns into a bastion of undead might.   ", d=34.320, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-330cd2db", h="330cd2db", t="The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves' holdings in the mountain's volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself.  ", d=30.868, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-33439fd8", h="33439fd8", t="Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal'ai's plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple's ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons. ", d=33.737, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-342c02c0", h="342c02c0", t="The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free.  ", d=27.811, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-4a0923b3", h="4a0923b3", t="Are you interested in exploring one of these dungeons?", d=3.327, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-4a6950fb", h="4a6950fb", t="The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.", d=3.801, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-4f48ef1f", h="4f48ef1f", t="Situated along the Zoram Strand of Ashenvale, Blackfathom Deeps was once a glorious temple dedicated to the night elves' moon-goddess Elune. However, the great Sundering shattered the temple - sinking it beneath the waves of the Veiled Sea. There it remained untouched - until, drawn by its ancient power - the naga and satyr emerged to plumb its secrets. Legends hold that the ancient beast, Aku'mai, has taken up residence within the temple's ruins.  ", d=31.701, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-581034a1", h="581034a1", t="The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ", d=32.427, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-5dc31760", h="5dc31760", t="During the War of the Ancients, the demigod Agamaggan came forth to battle the Burning Legion. The colossal boar was defeated, and over time in the areas where his blood fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted to life. The quilboar came to occupy these regions and hold them sacred. The heart of these massive thorn-colonies is the Razorfen. Razorfen Kraul was conquered by the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who some speculate has been negotiating with agents of the Scourge for some insidious purpose. ", d=35.595, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-5eccd4fa", h="5eccd4fa", t="The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.", d=6.408, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-5ff7a251", h="5ff7a251", t="Scarlet Monastery lies in the hills northeast of Tirisfal Glades.", d=5.478, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-66f64f6e", h="66f64f6e", t="Razorfen Kraul can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the west side of the road.", d=5.954, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-69040db4", h="69040db4", t="Love tokens are small messages of affection you can give to amorous town and city folk.  Such people will reward you with a gift of adoration.$B$BOr, if you are already adored by another, then at the least they'll give you a gift of friendship.", d=16.498, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-6a089d41", h="6a089d41", t="The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.", d=6.396, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-70185dce", h="70185dce", t="Uldaman can be found at the very northern end of the Badlands.", d=3.910, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-7b1bcef4", h="7b1bcef4", t="The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.", d=4.964, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-7de88db1", h="7de88db1", t="Located in Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan has been the gnomes' capital city for generations, though it was recently infested by mutant troggs. In a desperate attempt to retaliate, High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the emergency venting of the city's radioactive waste tanks. Though the troggs became irradiated, their siege continued unabated and the gnomes were forced to seek refuge in the dwarven city of Ironforge, where the High Tinker now enlists brave souls to help his people reclaim their beloved city.  ", d=34.066, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-864c5566", h="864c5566", t="The Wailing Caverns has its entrance at the Lushwater Oasis southwest of Crossroads in the Barrens.   ", d=6.857, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-95351c86", h="95351c86", t="Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat.  ", d=34.711, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-a9df0aa1", h="a9df0aa1", t="Blackfathom Deeps can be found at the north end of Zoram Strand along the coast of Ashenvale.", d=7.505, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-ab572ddf", h="ab572ddf", t="The monastery was once a center for learning and enlightenment. With the rise of the undead Scourge during the Third War, the peaceful Monastery was converted into a stronghold of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. The Crusaders are intolerant of all non-human races, regardless of alliance or affiliation. They believe that any and all outsiders are potential carriers of the undead plague - and must be destroyed.  ", d=29.771, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-ad5ec0ca", h="ad5ec0ca", t="No, I'm not, but lots of others are looking for love.  You should buy my love tokens, put on some cologne or perfume, and then pass them around!", d=11.043, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-adc7501c", h="adc7501c", t="The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.", d=8.021, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-b69e98a5", h="b69e98a5", t="If you put on cologne or perfume, then you'll see who is amorous.  Those are the ones who accept love tokens... and offer a gift in return.$B$BBut remember: to give someone a love token, you have to smell just right!  Men like the scent of perfume, while women prefer cologne.", d=19.226, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-b852ea17", h="b852ea17", t="Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm's fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade's existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council.  ", d=31.663, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-b8eefffb", h="b8eefffb", t="Shadowfang Keep is in southern Silverpine just north of Pyrewood Village.", d=5.515, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-b8ef9c65", h="b8ef9c65", t="The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.", d=4.501, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-c2bfa0cf", h="c2bfa0cf", t="Gnomeregan can be found in western Dun Morogh.", d=3.697, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-c80041d2", h="c80041d2", t="Welcome to my Inn, weary traveler. What can I do for you?", d=4.608, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-ca5fde90", h="ca5fde90", t="Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.", d=6.453, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-d352a290", h="d352a290", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook. ", d=28.646, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-e99614f5", h="e99614f5", t="The ruins of Zul'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.", d=5.673, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-f106f818", h="f106f818", t="Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara's most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres.  ", d=31.736, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-f2218c4a", h="f2218c4a", t="Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.", d=6.055, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-f88f28f5", h="f88f28f5", t="Ragefire Chasm can be found beneath the Shadow Cleft in the center of Orgrimmar.", d=6.055, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2352-f9fa0d11", h="f9fa0d11", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Cairne, Sylvanas and Thrall.", d=18.118, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[2357] = {
		{ f="2357-f8288f6c", h="f8288f6c", t="Years of quality breeding techniques and plenty of care allow me the privilege of showing you these horses!  Please, take your time as you consider them for your mount.  A horse is a companion for the ages, friend.  Don't sell yourself short - get your steed here today!", d=16.920, v="human-female-standard" },
		{ f="2357-fccbd4ef", h="fccbd4ef", t="Sorry, but I am not disposed to sell horses to any individual who is not considered to be at least exalted to the Kingdom of Stormwind.  These steeds are the finest you'll find anywhere, and we certainly wouldn't want them in the hands of our enemies.$B$BNot saying you're an enemy, of course... just earn the trust of Stormwind and then we can do business.", d=20.750, v="human-female-standard" },
	},
	[2367] = {
		{ f="2367-279d82d3", h="279d82d3", t="Your skill exceeds mine, though  I've heard that Old Man Heming in Booty Bay has copies of \"The Bass and You\".  That is sure to help you increase your skill.", d=11.539, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2367-837eac47", h="837eac47", t="You will need to find Nat Pagle in Dustwallow Marsh to get any better than you are currently.", d=6.450, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2367-c2467ddc", h="c2467ddc", t="I can teach you fishing skills.", d=2.648, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[2388] = {
		{ f="2388-03ca5480", h="03ca5480", t="Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.   ", d=30.390, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-174473b0", h="174473b0", t="Recently, a night elf druid named Naralex discovered a network of underground caverns within the heart of the Barrens. Believing he could use the caverns' springs to restore lushness to the Barrens, the druid began siphoning the energies of the fabled Emerald Dream. His vision somehow became a nightmare, however, and soon the Wailing Caverns changed into a den of vicious, deadly predators. It is said that Naralex still resides somewhere inside the labyrinth, trapped beyond the edges of the Emerald Dream.  ", d=41.910, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-17e9d243", h="17e9d243", t="Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world's creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone.  ", d=40.140, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-19490f29", h="19490f29", t="Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar's spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ", d=43.750, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-19cbe7de", h="19cbe7de", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Bolvar, Magni, or Tyrande.", d=27.280, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-1a6e2552", h="1a6e2552", t="This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul'Farrak's walls. ", d=35.066, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-22aa3fe4", h="22aa3fe4", t="Razorfen Downs can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the east side of the road.", d=9.400, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-2e88eda5", h="2e88eda5", t="Frustrated by the Dalaran wizards' lack of progress against the undead during the Third War, the Archmage Arugal elected to summon the extra-dimensional worgen to bolster his side's diminishing ranks. The wolf-men slaughtered the Scourge, then quickly turned on the wizards themselves and laid siege to the keep of the noble, Baron Silverlaine. The fort quickly fell into shadow and ruin. Driven mad with guilt, Arugal adopted the worgen as his children and retreated to the newly dubbed 'Shadowfang Keep'.  ", d=39.940, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-3141b27b", h="3141b27b", t="Crafted from the same vines as Razorfen Kraul, Razorfen Downs is the traditional capital city of the quilboar race. The sprawling, thorn-ridden labyrinth houses a veritable army of loyal quilboar as well as their high priests - the Death's Head tribe. Recently, however, a looming shadow has fallen over the crude den. Agents of the undead Scourge - led by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer - have taken control over the quilboar race and turned the maze of thorns into a bastion of undead might.   ", d=41.070, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-330cd2db", h="330cd2db", t="The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves' holdings in the mountain's volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself.  ", d=35.190, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-33439fd8", h="33439fd8", t="Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal'ai's plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple's ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons. ", d=43.190, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-342c02c0", h="342c02c0", t="The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free.  ", d=34.950, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-4a0923b3", h="4a0923b3", t="Are you interested in exploring one of these dungeons?", d=3.880, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-4a6950fb", h="4a6950fb", t="The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.", d=5.440, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-4f48ef1f", h="4f48ef1f", t="Situated along the Zoram Strand of Ashenvale, Blackfathom Deeps was once a glorious temple dedicated to the night elves' moon-goddess Elune. However, the great Sundering shattered the temple - sinking it beneath the waves of the Veiled Sea. There it remained untouched - until, drawn by its ancient power - the naga and satyr emerged to plumb its secrets. Legends hold that the ancient beast, Aku'mai, has taken up residence within the temple's ruins.  ", d=39.990, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-581034a1", h="581034a1", t="The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ", d=39.150, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-5dc31760", h="5dc31760", t="During the War of the Ancients, the demigod Agamaggan came forth to battle the Burning Legion. The colossal boar was defeated, and over time in the areas where his blood fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted to life. The quilboar came to occupy these regions and hold them sacred. The heart of these massive thorn-colonies is the Razorfen. Razorfen Kraul was conquered by the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who some speculate has been negotiating with agents of the Scourge for some insidious purpose. ", d=42.310, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-5eccd4fa", h="5eccd4fa", t="The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.", d=7.920, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-5ff7a251", h="5ff7a251", t="Scarlet Monastery lies in the hills northeast of Tirisfal Glades.", d=6.560, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-66f64f6e", h="66f64f6e", t="Razorfen Kraul can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the west side of the road.", d=8.360, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-69040db4", h="69040db4", t="Love tokens are small messages of affection you can give to amorous town and city folk.  Such people will reward you with a gift of adoration.$B$BOr, if you are already adored by another, then at the least they'll give you a gift of friendship.", d=20.360, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-6a089d41", h="6a089d41", t="The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.", d=6.360, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-70185dce", h="70185dce", t="Uldaman can be found at the very northern end of the Badlands.", d=6.160, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-7b1bcef4", h="7b1bcef4", t="The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.", d=8.040, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-7de88db1", h="7de88db1", t="Located in Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan has been the gnomes' capital city for generations, though it was recently infested by mutant troggs. In a desperate attempt to retaliate, High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the emergency venting of the city's radioactive waste tanks. Though the troggs became irradiated, their siege continued unabated and the gnomes were forced to seek refuge in the dwarven city of Ironforge, where the High Tinker now enlists brave souls to help his people reclaim their beloved city.  ", d=39.870, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-864c5566", h="864c5566", t="The Wailing Caverns has its entrance at the Lushwater Oasis southwest of Crossroads in the Barrens.   ", d=7.920, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-95351c86", h="95351c86", t="Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat.  ", d=39.990, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-a9df0aa1", h="a9df0aa1", t="Blackfathom Deeps can be found at the north end of Zoram Strand along the coast of Ashenvale.", d=9.160, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-ab572ddf", h="ab572ddf", t="The monastery was once a center for learning and enlightenment. With the rise of the undead Scourge during the Third War, the peaceful Monastery was converted into a stronghold of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. The Crusaders are intolerant of all non-human races, regardless of alliance or affiliation. They believe that any and all outsiders are potential carriers of the undead plague - and must be destroyed.  ", d=32.030, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-ad5ec0ca", h="ad5ec0ca", t="No, I'm not, but lots of others are looking for love.  You should buy my love tokens, put on some cologne or perfume, and then pass them around!", d=11.200, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-adc7501c", h="adc7501c", t="The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.", d=9.400, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-b69e98a5", h="b69e98a5", t="If you put on cologne or perfume, then you'll see who is amorous.  Those are the ones who accept love tokens... and offer a gift in return.$B$BBut remember: to give someone a love token, you have to smell just right!  Men like the scent of perfume, while women prefer cologne.", d=26.800, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-b852ea17", h="b852ea17", t="Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm's fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade's existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council.  ", d=40.910, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-b8eefffb", h="b8eefffb", t="Shadowfang Keep is in southern Silverpine just north of Pyrewood Village.", d=8.480, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-b8ef9c65", h="b8ef9c65", t="The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.", d=5.000, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-c2bfa0cf", h="c2bfa0cf", t="Gnomeregan can be found in western Dun Morogh.", d=5.080, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-ca5fde90", h="ca5fde90", t="Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.", d=9.400, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-d352a290", h="d352a290", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook. ", d=38.190, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-e99614f5", h="e99614f5", t="The ruins of Zul'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.", d=6.200, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-f106f818", h="f106f818", t="Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara's most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres.  ", d=34.470, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-f2218c4a", h="f2218c4a", t="Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.", d=7.080, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-f88f28f5", h="f88f28f5", t="Ragefire Chasm can be found beneath the Shadow Cleft in the center of Orgrimmar.", d=7.480, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-f9fa0d11", h="f9fa0d11", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Cairne, Sylvanas and Thrall.", d=24.280, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2388-fde1fb79", h="fde1fb79", t="Rest your weary bones for a spell.", d=4.160, v="scourge-male-standard" },
	},
	[2389] = {
		{ f="2389-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=3.160, v="scourge-female-standard" },
	},
	[2391] = {
		{ f="2391-11012350", h="11012350", t="Another student. Wonderful. This is why Lydon belongs to the Royal Society of Snobs and gets to do research, and I'm stuck being an instructor. If I win another teaching award, I'll never live it down!", d=17.960, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2391-5dffcf15", h="5dffcf15", t="Another interruption. How am I supposed to get any work done like this? Don't answer that; do I look as if I care what you have to say? Why don't you go bother Mr. High-And-Mighty instead?", d=18.680, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2391-9a18bb90", h="9a18bb90", t="Me, train you? Come on--we both know I can't. It's this teaching, you see. My own skills suffer. You want training, go to Doctor Herbert Halsey, a Forsaken in the Apothecarium of the Undercity.", d=19.040, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2391-d1d4b01c", h="d1d4b01c", t="Don't waste my time. I have research projects older than you. Go talk to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium of the Undercity. He's a Forsaken who can probably manage to teach you the basics.", d=17.360, v="scourge-male-standard" },
	},
	[2393] = {
		{ f="2393-e26243eb", h="e26243eb", t="Can I show you what I have for sale?    ", d=3.520, v="scourge-male-dark" },
	},
	[2399] = {
		{ f="2399-536469cb", h="536469cb", t="The place is a bit drafty... but what do I care? I'm dead.", d=5.800, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2399-728032b3", h="728032b3", t="Who sent you here? You're not ready for my instruction yet! You'll be told when you're ready.", d=9.000, v="scourge-male-standard" },
		{ f="2399-c01b98a0", h="c01b98a0", t="You're doing very well in the art of tailoring, I must admit. Now, let's see how good you REALLY are...", d=8.880, v="scourge-male-standard" },
	},
	[2409] = {
		{ f="2409-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.080, v="human-female-warrior" },
	},
	[2410] = {
		{ f="2410-8b3451aa", h="8b3451aa", t="My studies take me far from the Under City, but to truly learn one must be near to the source of knowledge.", d=10.400, v="scourge-male-dark" },
	},
	[2425] = {
		{ f="2425-7dca81fc", h="7dca81fc", t="Do not presume to speak to me as though you are my equal, $c. Sylvanas is my queen, and I will do as she bids.  If you do not show the proper respect, I assure you, we can find a more than suitable place for you in the Nether.  But there is no reason we cannot have words if you wish to aid the Dark Lady...", d=23.470, v="npc-11658" },
	},
	[2432] = {
		{ f="2432-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.080, v="human-female-official", s={ ["m"]=2.231 } },
	},
	[2455] = {
		{ f="2455-105cd232", h="105cd232", t="No one's ever stolen anything out of here. Not in the whole history of... the whole history!", d=6.280, v="human-female-standard" },
		{ f="2455-2237a3b1", h="2237a3b1", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us sir?", d=9.400, v="human-female-standard" },
		{ f="2455-34824363", h="34824363", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us $g sir : ma'am;?", d=11.320, v="human-female-standard", g=true },
		{ f="2455-6928abbf", h="6928abbf", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us ma'am?", d=9.480, v="human-female-standard" },
	},
	[2456] = {
		{ f="2456-105cd232", h="105cd232", t="No one's ever stolen anything out of here. Not in the whole history of... the whole history!", d=6.383, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2456-2237a3b1", h="2237a3b1", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us sir?", d=10.273, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="2456-34824363", h="34824363", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us $g sir : ma'am;?", d=10.273, v="human-male-standard", g=true },
	},
	[2457] = {
		{ f="2457-105cd232", h="105cd232", t="No one's ever stolen anything out of here. Not in the whole history of... the whole history!", d=6.182, v="human-male-official" },
		{ f="2457-2237a3b1", h="2237a3b1", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us sir?", d=9.560, v="human-male-official" },
		{ f="2457-34824363", h="34824363", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us $g sir : ma'am;?", d=9.446, v="human-male-official", g=true },
		{ f="2457-6928abbf", h="6928abbf", t="Welcome to the Bank of Stormwind. We offer financial accounts and safety deposit boxes for valuable items. Do you already have an account with us ma'am?", d=7.956, v="human-male-official" },
	},
	[2481] = {
		{ f="2481-014b9d07", h="014b9d07", t="A customer all the way out here? What luck! This place was a goldmine of empty alchemy bottles. Kinda weird.    Don't worry, I washed 'em out.", d=10.448, v="human-male" },
	},
	[2485] = {
		{ f="2485-1c7cd7a4", h="1c7cd7a4", t="I do not believe you possess the mental acuity to grasp the nature of portal magic.", d=6.480, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="2485-6e89a35a", h="6e89a35a", t="As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place.  I can teach you if you are ready.", d=10.720, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="2485-aa6f2374", h="aa6f2374", t="As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place.  I can teach you if you are ready.", d=10.280, v="human-female-official" },
	},
	[2489] = {
		{ f="2489-1c7cd7a4", h="1c7cd7a4", t="I do not believe you possess the mental acuity to grasp the nature of portal magic.", d=4.172, v="gnome-male-standard" },
		{ f="2489-6e89a35a", h="6e89a35a", t="As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place.  I can teach you if you are ready.", d=7.462, v="gnome-male-standard" },
		{ f="2489-aa6f2374", h="aa6f2374", t="As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place.  I can teach you if you are ready.", d=6.626, v="gnome-male-standard" },
	},
	[2492] = {
		{ f="2492-1c7cd7a4", h="1c7cd7a4", t="I do not believe you possess the mental acuity to grasp the nature of portal magic.", d=7.000, v="scourge-male-warrior" },
		{ f="2492-6e89a35a", h="6e89a35a", t="As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place.  I can teach you if you are ready.", d=10.320, v="scourge-male-warrior" },
		{ f="2492-aa6f2374", h="aa6f2374", t="As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place.  I can teach you if you are ready.", d=11.480, v="scourge-male-warrior" },
	},
	[2496] = {
		{ f="2496-e386ad41", h="e386ad41", t="Welcome to Booty Bay, partner.  I hope your stay in my town is enjoyable and uneventful - emphasis on the latter.  We've got plenty of drink if you're thirsty, and plenty of bouncers if you're antsy.$B$BNow then... what can this humble servant of the Steamwheedle Cartel do for you?  Better still - what can you do for me, eh?", d=18.350, v="npc-7167" },
	},
	[2504] = {
		{ f="2504-60988031", h="60988031", t="Please clean yourself before handling our tomes.", d=3.514, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[2543] = {
		{ f="2543-41cbc7e1", h="41cbc7e1", t="Take care while in our city, $c. We are ever wary of strangers since the city was destroyed, and any untoward behavior while within this place will not be tolerated.", d=9.106, v="human-male-official" },
		{ f="2543-912d8d1d", h="912d8d1d", t="As a member of the High Order of shen'dorei, you are most welcome here in our city, $c.     Your leader, Elaadrin Evengale and I have had quite the correspondence these recent months. I feel that the Kirin Tor and the High Order are cut from the same cloth, always in search of answers to the greater mysteries of the world. Now more than ever, seeking said answers is vital to all of our survival.    Just as you have experienced an interruption in your way of life on Zephras, the flow of magic on Azeroth has been chaotic as well. Disturbed, somehow... as if a rock has been dropped into still water, causing ripples to surge across the surface.    Ah, but talk of such troubles can wait for another time. For now, welcome to Azeroth.", d=43.863, v="human-male-official" },
	},
	[2627] = {
		{ f="2627-08d0d148", h="08d0d148", t="Yeah, you know a few things! If you wanna' learn more you're gonna' have to talk to Georgio Bolero in Stormwind.", d=6.106, v="goblin-male-zany" },
		{ f="2627-834549b8", h="834549b8", t="Not bad... for an amateur! Still, you know about as much as I do. If you wanna' learn more you're gonna' have to talk to Josef Gregorian in Undercity.", d=9.189, v="goblin-male-zany" },
		{ f="2627-9771bc6e", h="9771bc6e", t="Well well, not too bad. Maybe I CAN show you a few things...", d=4.479, v="goblin-male-zany" },
		{ f="2627-dbf4383b", h="dbf4383b", t="They say a stitch in time saves... what, eleven? Ah, I can't remember. Stupid saying anyway.", d=5.578, v="goblin-male-zany" },
	},
	[2670] = {
		{ f="2670-4b80d68c", h="4b80d68c", t="Welcome to my shop, $c. What is it the Goodstitch brothers can do for you?", d=5.677, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="2670-9326f7e7", h="9326f7e7", t="Ah, one of my favorite customers. You look to be of a warlock of some power, $n. I am pleased to meet you. If there is anything I can do for you, please, just ask.$B$BMy brother and I feel that it will be your kind who lead us into the next great era. One with such power... such control... it's only a matter of time before the Legion itself bends to your will.$B$BI am but a little envious.", d=32.778, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[2704] = {
		{ f="2704-15da2919", h="15da2919", t="Heya mon.  You come right place learn how ta wield a new weapon.", d=5.240, v="troll-male-dark" },
		{ f="2704-f0975974", h="f0975974", t="Ansekhwa, da tauren weapon master, is on da Thunder Bluff lower rise.  He teach one and two-handed maces, staves and guns.    Archibald, da undead weapon master in da War Quarter of da Undercity, train good with crossbows, daggers, one and two-handed swords and polearms.    Sayoc, da ugly orc right here, can teach da ways of bows, daggers, fist weapons, one and two-handed axes and thrown weapons mon.", d=34.590, v="troll-male-dark" },
	},
	[2706] = {
		{ f="2706-368f0fed", h="368f0fed", t="Thanks to the Warchief, even here in the ruins of our former prison, some hope remains, and the Horde rises anew.", d=7.520, v="troll-male-shaman" },
	},
	[2733] = {
		{ f="2733-10e876c3", h="10e876c3", t="Are you here to make a contribution to research?     Do you have any limbs you're willing to part with?", d=8.000, v="scourge-male-dark" },
	},
	[2784] = {
		{ f="2784-970770be", h="970770be", t="Ah, so you have. You are most welcome in Ironforge, $c.     This city is the seat of the Bronzebeard Clan. We are an ancient and proud people and our craftsmen are second to none. You'll find no finer creations of metal or stonework than those of dwarven-make.    We are also amongst the boldest of explorers on Azeroth. If you have a taste for adventure, you will be in good company amongst our people.    Thank you for speaking with me, $N. Go now with the blessings of the Bronzebeard Clan.     I wish you and your people well.", d=41.030, v="npc-3597" },
		{ f="2784-a2f26445", h="a2f26445", t="Ah, so you have. You are most welcome in Ironforge, $c.     This city is the seat of the Bronzebeard Clan. We are an ancient and proud people and our craftsmen are second to none. You'll find no finer creations of metal or stonework than dwarven-make.    We are also amongst boldest of explorers on Azeroth. If you have a taste for adventure, you will be in good company amongst our people.    Thank you for speaking with me, $N. Go now with the blessings of the Bronzebeard Clan.     I wish you and your people well.", d=39.910, v="npc-3597" },
		{ f="2784-a5c53ddf", h="a5c53ddf", t="Welcome to Ironforge, $c.", d=4.080, v="npc-3597" },
	},
	[2786] = {
		{ f="2786-c9907ea0", h="c9907ea0", t="Welcome to Bonegrip's Runes and Dooms, $c.  You may look, but do not touch.  Some of the knowledge here is not meant for the...uninitiated.", d=9.040, v="dwarf-male-grim" },
	},
	[2788] = {
		{ f="2788-08259375", h="08259375", t="Hello, $N. Welcome to Refuge Pointe.", d=3.885, v="human-male-official" },
		{ f="2788-109efbc8", h="109efbc8", t="Don't mind Skuerto, $n. He doesn't mean to be rude, he's just terribly busy. While we wait for him to finish scouting, why don't we work on something more productive?", d=8.381, v="human-male-official" },
	},
	[2798] = {
		{ f="2798-34baaaf3", h="34baaaf3", t="Only the renowned Doctor Gregory Victor can improve your skill now.  He can be found in Arathi Highlands at Hammerfall.", d=10.680, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
		{ f="2798-43457c57", h="43457c57", t="Balai Lok'Wein of Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh sells a manual that you will need to study in order to improve your skills!", d=9.480, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
		{ f="2798-a28d29e1", h="a28d29e1", t="I can train you in First Aid techniques.", d=3.720, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
	},
	[2804] = {
		{ f="2804-7e5b36ab", h="7e5b36ab", t="I am sorry $c, but you are not seasoned enough yet to enter Warsong Gulch.", d=8.920, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="2804-cda4c0c1", h="cda4c0c1", t="Are you here to fight for us at Warsong Gulch?  Lok'tar Ogar $c!", d=6.520, v="orc-male-guard" },
	},
	[2817] = {
		{ f="2817-de8ac2c8", h="de8ac2c8", t="You must be hard up to be wandering these Badlands, $c.  Hard up like me.  Or maybe you're here because you're crazy.  Crazy, like me.", d=10.833, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[2834] = {
		{ f="2834-279d82d3", h="279d82d3", t="Your skill exceeds mine, though  I've heard that Old Man Heming in Booty Bay has copies of \"The Bass and You\".  That is sure to help you increase your skill.", d=11.120, v="goblin-male-guard" },
		{ f="2834-837eac47", h="837eac47", t="You will need to find Nat Pagle in Dustwallow Marsh to get any better than you are currently.", d=6.040, v="goblin-male-guard" },
		{ f="2834-c2467ddc", h="c2467ddc", t="I can teach you fishing skills.", d=2.360, v="goblin-male-guard" },
	},
	[2835] = {
		{ f="2835-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.239, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[2836] = {
		{ f="2836-9643d624", h="9643d624", t="Yeah? Of course I'm a smith. What, you think Dwarves are the only ones worth their weight in anvils? Fine, be that way. Go get a dwarf to help you!", d=11.053, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="2836-c3243b92", h="c3243b92", t="Are you kidding me? You must be kidding me! Either that or you think I'm a clown here to amuse you. Is that what you think? That I'm a clown? Huh, is it! You think I'm a clown don't you!", d=13.988, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="2836-fa0f2570", h="fa0f2570", t="You act like this is the best junk I've ever seen. Sure it's ok, but I see stuff this 'OK' every day. Tell you what, you find a way to wow me, and I'll teach you things that make dwarves smile in their sleep.", d=13.279, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[2837] = {
		{ f="2837-4a119c04", h="4a119c04", t="You're better at this gig than I am! You want someone with even more experience than I've got. That'd be Ainethil, a night elf lady who lives in the Craftsmen's Terrace of Darnassus.", d=12.386, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="2837-67bfe795", h="67bfe795", t="Glyx and I have an understanding: he keeps me supplied, and I keep him rich. Seriously! What that pirate charges me for a measly pouch of crumpled kingsblood... it's enough to make a grown goblin cry.", d=14.123, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="2837-a731830b", h="a731830b", t="I've got plenty of great recipes for you to take a look at, and at discounted prices, too!", d=6.962, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="2837-b365ca74", h="b365ca74", t="You're better at this gig than I am! You want someone with even more experience than I've got. That'd be Doctor Herbert Halsey, an undead who works in the Apothecarium of the Undercity.", d=11.367, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[2851] = {
		{ f="2851-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.360, v="orc-female-standard" },
	},
	[2855] = {
		{ f="2855-1c3f5d2d", h="1c3f5d2d", t="We use many animal pelts and skins in our creations. ", d=4.556, v="orc-male-standard" },
		{ f="2855-774f3757", h="774f3757", t="I will teach you what I can.", d=2.441, v="orc-male-standard" },
		{ f="2855-8f48a40a", h="8f48a40a", t="I know a few things, but I'm no expert. Lucky for you, Magar is. He's standing near the back of the shop. See if he can help you, but be careful not to rile him. He can be irritable.", d=14.530, v="orc-male-standard" },
	},
	[2857] = {
		{ f="2857-31f4573e", h="31f4573e", t="You know who's really smart? Nogg! Smarter than me, even. You go tell Nogg Thund sent you! You can find him by the control panel over there.", d=13.920, v="orc-male-shady" },
		{ f="2857-6139c96a", h="6139c96a", t="Who says Orcs aren't smart? It takes a lot of brains to be an engineer!", d=5.560, v="orc-male-shady" },
		{ f="2857-829e343d", h="829e343d", t="You think you're smart enough? You think you got what it takes? Let's find out!", d=6.360, v="orc-male-shady" },
	},
	[2858] = {
		{ f="2858-d37b59d0", h="d37b59d0", t="How may I be of service?", d=3.316, v="orc-male-standard" },
	},
	[2859] = {
		{ f="2859-2cc67a59", h="2cc67a59", t="Fastest gryphons this side of Aerie Peak. Want to take a ride?", d=4.240, v="dwarf-male-grim" },
	},
	[2861] = {
		{ f="2861-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=1.933, v="orc-male-standard" },
	},
	[2878] = {
		{ f="2878-0e051c59", h="0e051c59", t="You've come for training in order to pass it on to your pets?", d=3.170, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
		{ f="2878-4ef1d72e", h="4ef1d72e", t="Ah friend, I only help hunters and their pets.", d=3.307, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
	},
	[2879] = {
		{ f="2879-0e051c59", h="0e051c59", t="You've come for training in order to pass it on to your pets?", d=3.080, v="dwarf-female-young" },
		{ f="2879-4ef1d72e", h="4ef1d72e", t="Ah friend, I only help hunters and their pets.", d=3.440, v="dwarf-female-young" },
	},
	[2913] = {
		{ f="2913-5112b624", h="5112b624", t="Who would have guessed the excavation would have uncovered such findings!", d=5.304, v="dwarf-female-guard" },
		{ f="2913-fa848faf", h="fa848faf", t="Oh, $N! It's you! I wasn't sure when you'd come back.    What did Tarrel say? Did he... say anything?", d=9.570, v="dwarf-female-guard" },
	},
	[2916] = {
		{ f="2916-427db4a9", h="427db4a9", t="Welcome to the Explorer's League.  If you need information, and it is in book form, then I might be able to help you out.", d=6.760, v="dwarf-male-grim" },
	},
	[2930] = {
		{ f="2930-cd94cda6", h="cd94cda6", t="Corruption sneaks into nature's grove.  The forest must be protected at all costs.", d=8.108, v="nightelf-female-sentinel" },
	},
	[2934] = {
		{ f="2934-2cd97b51", h="2cd97b51", t="Knowledge is both tool and weapon to those with the will to use it.", d=4.280, v="scourge-male-dark", s={ ["f"]=5.440 } },
	},
	[2941] = {
		{ f="2941-ad5aada3", h="ad5aada3", t="Thorium Brotherhood or not, if one of them Dark Iron gets near to me they'll taste my mattock up the side of their head!  Now, where can I send ya $G lad : lass;?", d=9.360, v="dwarf-female-young", g=true },
	},
	[2943] = {
		{ f="2943-e0a94ace", h="e0a94ace", t="Hail $c. Didn't I see you recently at an exclusive gathering? You look familiar, but then again this city is a busy place.$B$BIf you attended that convention, then surely you were given a secret code. Tell me your code and I will give you a special prize in return.", d=15.160, v="dwarf-male-grim" },
	},
	[2980] = {
		{ f="2980-e775a01e", h="e775a01e", t="Greetings, $N, and welcome to Camp Narache. News of your arrival spread quickly among the tribe.", d=7.002, v="tauren-male-warrior" },
	},
	[2981] = {
		{ f="2981-72360bcb", h="72360bcb", t="Hail, $c. In my years I have seen many eager $r who wish to prove their worth to the tribe. It should not be forgotten that eagerness is no substitute for wisdom and experience.", d=17.120, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[2988] = {
		{ f="2988-00c35128", h="00c35128", t="The Outrunners' duty is to ensure the safety of those who travel across the plains of Mulgore. Those that would threaten the safety of the $r homeland risk punishment at our hands.", d=11.108, v="tauren-male-warrior" },
		{ f="2988-2e223ff7", h="2e223ff7", t="The Outrunners' duty is to ensure the safety of those who travel across the plains of Mulgore. Those that would threaten the safety of the tauren homeland risk punishment at our hands.", d=11.386, v="tauren-male-warrior" },
	},
	[2993] = {
		{ f="2993-f7a5deb4", h="f7a5deb4", t="The land has been good to our people, $c. We must be thankful for our good fortune.", d=8.000, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[2995] = {
		{ f="2995-bfaf54b7", h="bfaf54b7", t="When mounted on the back of a wind rider, one sees that its reputation for strength and speed is well earned.", d=6.167, v="tauren-male-warrior" },
	},
	[2998] = {
		{ f="2998-19ec09c0", h="19ec09c0", t="Everything has a spirit, if you learn to listen to it you can get it to take any shape you want. Blacksmithing isn't about beating metal, forcing it to do your will. It's about listening to the spirit within the steel and guiding it to the shape you know it wants to take.", d=20.080, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="2998-1b89f16f", h="1b89f16f", t="You have the look of a $g man : woman; who seeks knowledge. Perhaps you seek the teachings of the forge, and the hammer. Perhaps I can guide you down that path. But only once you have accepted the spirits, and listened to their calling.", d=18.400, v="tauren-male-elder", g=true },
		{ f="2998-d12d69b6", h="d12d69b6", t="You have learned much, but I sense that there is more left for the spirits to teach you. I can place your foot on the path but cannot guide your steps. Go and find Saru Steelfury in Orgrimmar, the next stretch of your journey begins there.", d=22.720, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[3001] = {
		{ f="3001-58405dcd", h="58405dcd", t="Greetings.", d=1.400, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[3004] = {
		{ f="3004-3236d362", h="3236d362", t="Aren't the patterns beautiful? Each one speaks with its own voice.", d=5.160, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3004-97845caa", h="97845caa", t="There are fundamental things you must learn before I can aid you. Speak to my apprentice, Vhan. He is kind and patient and will teach you what you need to know.", d=11.720, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3004-a2273ec5", h="a2273ec5", t="My knowledge is limited, though I am still learning. It is time for you to move on, traveler. Find Josef Gregorian in Undercity and tell him you are ready.", d=13.560, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3004-dfa12b04", h="dfa12b04", t="You are truly a determined student. I will be happy to provide you with instruction!", d=7.440, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
	},
	[3007] = {
		{ f="3007-501c3600", h="501c3600", t="Cairne has brought us to a land rich with possibilities for the future. We have been fortunate, and so in turn we pass on our good fortune to others. That is why I began teaching, $N.", d=15.840, v="tauren-female-standard" },
		{ f="3007-6f1fdfed", h="6f1fdfed", t="The needle is small, but the thread is strong, and the stitches are fine. Our pact with Thrall and the others will hold. The Horde will not be driven from these lands.", d=12.880, v="tauren-female-standard" },
		{ f="3007-b65785f5", h="b65785f5", t="It's been so long since I was a novice myself that I don't think I'd be the best teacher for you. Try talking to Tarn or Mak, right over there. One of them should be able to answer your questions.", d=14.480, v="tauren-female-standard" },
		{ f="3007-c9ecec7c", h="c9ecec7c", t="Even my talents have a limit, and you have reached it. Congratulations, $n. Your next stop should be Camp Mojache in Feralas. The tauren Hahrana Ironhide lives there; she is renowned for her skill.", d=17.760, v="tauren-female-standard" },
	},
	[3008] = {
		{ f="3008-a1a91c02", h="a1a91c02", t="Cairne himself lives here, they say. Once I have finished crafting a fitting gift, I will seek him out. Perhaps he will have words of wisdom for me.", d=12.040, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="3008-b0fd68db", h="b0fd68db", t="Cleanse your hands before you begin any project. Staining the leather with blood or dirt would take away from its natural beauty.", d=10.200, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="3008-d055944a", h="d055944a", t="Your talent is beyond my own, friend. Speak with Tarn here; his knowledge of leather is much greater than mine. I'm sure he would welcome another student.", d=13.360, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[3009] = {
		{ f="3009-23b0a36f", h="23b0a36f", t="I cannot in good conscience spend time training novices while our allies, the undead, are suffering so terribly. Please speak with Kray over there instead; he can help you for now.", d=12.440, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3009-28255eab", h="28255eab", t="Your potion-making skills are beyond mine. Seek out the undead Doctor Herbert Halsey in the Apothecarium of the Undercity. He has the skill to train you further, and you can witness firsthand his people's plight.", d=15.800, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3009-490d29e8", h="490d29e8", t="Can you not sense the anguish of the Earth Mother for her lost children, the undead? Speak quickly, $N. Every second costs me dearly. We must help them find their way back to her!", d=14.720, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3009-a7458c5c", h="a7458c5c", t="When I first saw the undead, I wept, for I could not imagine their horror and loneliness. The Earth Mother spoke to me then; she sang in my blood. And she told me, \"Save them.\"", d=13.720, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
	},
	[3011] = {
		{ f="3011-257b9f8a", h="257b9f8a", t="Surely Mot didn't send you to me? He knows better. You are not yet capable of understanding what I would teach you. See my son Mot, just outside there, and finish training with him. ", d=14.240, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
		{ f="3011-463ccfcd", h="463ccfcd", t="Enchanting has run in our family for generations. I learned at an early age, just as my son is doing now.", d=9.160, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
		{ f="3011-893e8e5b", h="893e8e5b", t="There is one whose knowledge exceeds my own. You are ready to seek her out. Go to Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon Mountains. Find Hgarth, and continue your training.", d=15.080, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
		{ f="3011-ab001504", h="ab001504", t="Ah, very good. I am satisfied that you are a worthy student. Now, your training with me may begin...", d=8.480, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
		{ f="3011-dab22e8f", h="dab22e8f", t="I will teach you... soon. I require a demonstration of your loyalty, first.", d=6.960, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
	},
	[3026] = {
		{ f="3026-0c543544", h="0c543544", t="Cooking is a life long pursuit and I see we share the same passion!", d=6.000, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3026-3b48d638", h="3b48d638", t="Dirge Quikcleave of Gadgetzan is a master of the culinary arts.  To better yourself you will need to seek him out.", d=9.360, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3026-48c1c064", h="48c1c064", t="Wulan in Shadowprey Village can sell you the \"Expert Cookbook\".  You will need that if you are to better yourself.", d=8.760, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3026-b48f927f", h="b48f927f", t="I can teach you how to cook!", d=2.600, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
	},
	[3028] = {
		{ f="3028-279d82d3", h="279d82d3", t="Your skill exceeds mine, though  I've heard that Old Man Heming in Booty Bay has copies of \"The Bass and You\".  That is sure to help you increase your skill.", d=14.120, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="3028-837eac47", h="837eac47", t="You will need to find Nat Pagle in Dustwallow Marsh to get any better than you are currently.", d=7.040, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="3028-c2467ddc", h="c2467ddc", t="I can teach you fishing skills.", d=2.920, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[3030] = {
		{ f="3030-08830bac", h="08830bac", t="Through rigorous retraining I have had to break many students of all they had previously learned so that I might teach them anew.  The service I offer becomes increasingly difficult to perform each time it is done.  It is for that reason that it becomes increasingly expensive with each retraining.  Do you desire that I break you of the talents you have learned?", d=25.830, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3030-1605f087", h="1605f087", t="The spirits have guided you to me. How may I be of service?", d=5.440, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3030-8fca8484", h="8fca8484", t="If you desire, in addition to training, I have it within my power to erase the knowledge of your talents from your mind.  Be warned that every time you undergo this procedure the more difficult it is to perform, and therefore the more expensive it becomes.", d=16.000, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="3030-996eca9b", h="996eca9b", t="May the spirits be with you.", d=2.240, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
	},
