		{ f="7737-b69e98a5", h="b69e98a5", t="If you put on cologne or perfume, then you'll see who is amorous.  Those are the ones who accept love tokens... and offer a gift in return.$B$BBut remember: to give someone a love token, you have to smell just right!  Men like the scent of perfume, while women prefer cologne.", d=19.360, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-b852ea17", h="b852ea17", t="Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm's fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade's existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council.  ", d=36.350, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-b8eefffb", h="b8eefffb", t="Shadowfang Keep is in southern Silverpine just north of Pyrewood Village.", d=6.240, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-b8ef9c65", h="b8ef9c65", t="The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.", d=5.400, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-c2bfa0cf", h="c2bfa0cf", t="Gnomeregan can be found in western Dun Morogh.", d=4.400, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-ca5fde90", h="ca5fde90", t="Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.", d=7.320, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-d352a290", h="d352a290", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook. ", d=33.590, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-e013de07", h="e013de07", t="As the wind on the plains, you are always welcome here.", d=4.360, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-e99614f5", h="e99614f5", t="The ruins of Zul'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.", d=7.360, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-f106f818", h="f106f818", t="Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara's most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres.  ", d=31.470, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-f2218c4a", h="f2218c4a", t="Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.", d=7.440, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-f88f28f5", h="f88f28f5", t="Ragefire Chasm can be found beneath the Shadow Cleft in the center of Orgrimmar.", d=5.520, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
		{ f="7737-f9fa0d11", h="f9fa0d11", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Cairne, Sylvanas and Thrall.", d=20.280, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
	},
	[7744] = {
		{ f="7744-03ca5480", h="03ca5480", t="Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.   ", d=29.510, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-174473b0", h="174473b0", t="Recently, a night elf druid named Naralex discovered a network of underground caverns within the heart of the Barrens. Believing he could use the caverns' springs to restore lushness to the Barrens, the druid began siphoning the energies of the fabled Emerald Dream. His vision somehow became a nightmare, however, and soon the Wailing Caverns changed into a den of vicious, deadly predators. It is said that Naralex still resides somewhere inside the labyrinth, trapped beyond the edges of the Emerald Dream.  ", d=31.590, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-17e9d243", h="17e9d243", t="Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world's creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone.  ", d=33.140, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-19490f29", h="19490f29", t="Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar's spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ", d=34.270, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-19cbe7de", h="19cbe7de", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Bolvar, Magni, or Tyrande.", d=19.280, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-1a6e2552", h="1a6e2552", t="This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul'Farrak's walls. ", d=27.430, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-22aa3fe4", h="22aa3fe4", t="Razorfen Downs can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the east side of the road.", d=5.840, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-2e88eda5", h="2e88eda5", t="Frustrated by the Dalaran wizards' lack of progress against the undead during the Third War, the Archmage Arugal elected to summon the extra-dimensional worgen to bolster his side's diminishing ranks. The wolf-men slaughtered the Scourge, then quickly turned on the wizards themselves and laid siege to the keep of the noble, Baron Silverlaine. The fort quickly fell into shadow and ruin. Driven mad with guilt, Arugal adopted the worgen as his children and retreated to the newly dubbed 'Shadowfang Keep'.  ", d=32.220, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-3141b27b", h="3141b27b", t="Crafted from the same vines as Razorfen Kraul, Razorfen Downs is the traditional capital city of the quilboar race. The sprawling, thorn-ridden labyrinth houses a veritable army of loyal quilboar as well as their high priests - the Death's Head tribe. Recently, however, a looming shadow has fallen over the crude den. Agents of the undead Scourge - led by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer - have taken control over the quilboar race and turned the maze of thorns into a bastion of undead might.   ", d=34.910, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-330cd2db", h="330cd2db", t="The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves' holdings in the mountain's volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself.  ", d=28.630, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-33439fd8", h="33439fd8", t="Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal'ai's plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple's ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons. ", d=31.710, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-342c02c0", h="342c02c0", t="The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free.  ", d=27.470, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-4a0923b3", h="4a0923b3", t="Are you interested in exploring one of these dungeons?", d=3.880, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-4a6950fb", h="4a6950fb", t="The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.", d=3.840, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-4f48ef1f", h="4f48ef1f", t="Situated along the Zoram Strand of Ashenvale, Blackfathom Deeps was once a glorious temple dedicated to the night elves' moon-goddess Elune. However, the great Sundering shattered the temple - sinking it beneath the waves of the Veiled Sea. There it remained untouched - until, drawn by its ancient power - the naga and satyr emerged to plumb its secrets. Legends hold that the ancient beast, Aku'mai, has taken up residence within the temple's ruins.  ", d=32.990, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-581034a1", h="581034a1", t="The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ", d=35.910, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-5dc31760", h="5dc31760", t="During the War of the Ancients, the demigod Agamaggan came forth to battle the Burning Legion. The colossal boar was defeated, and over time in the areas where his blood fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted to life. The quilboar came to occupy these regions and hold them sacred. The heart of these massive thorn-colonies is the Razorfen. Razorfen Kraul was conquered by the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who some speculate has been negotiating with agents of the Scourge for some insidious purpose. ", d=34.590, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-5eccd4fa", h="5eccd4fa", t="The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.", d=5.800, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-5ff7a251", h="5ff7a251", t="Scarlet Monastery lies in the hills northeast of Tirisfal Glades.", d=4.440, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-66f64f6e", h="66f64f6e", t="Razorfen Kraul can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the west side of the road.", d=6.280, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-69040db4", h="69040db4", t="Love tokens are small messages of affection you can give to amorous town and city folk.  Such people will reward you with a gift of adoration.$B$BOr, if you are already adored by another, then at the least they'll give you a gift of friendship.", d=14.440, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-6a089d41", h="6a089d41", t="The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.", d=6.000, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-70185dce", h="70185dce", t="Uldaman can be found at the very northern end of the Badlands.", d=3.840, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-7b1bcef4", h="7b1bcef4", t="The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.", d=5.080, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-7de88db1", h="7de88db1", t="Located in Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan has been the gnomes' capital city for generations, though it was recently infested by mutant troggs. In a desperate attempt to retaliate, High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the emergency venting of the city's radioactive waste tanks. Though the troggs became irradiated, their siege continued unabated and the gnomes were forced to seek refuge in the dwarven city of Ironforge, where the High Tinker now enlists brave souls to help his people reclaim their beloved city.  ", d=31.070, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-864c5566", h="864c5566", t="The Wailing Caverns has its entrance at the Lushwater Oasis southwest of Crossroads in the Barrens.   ", d=6.480, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-95351c86", h="95351c86", t="Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat.  ", d=33.870, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-a9df0aa1", h="a9df0aa1", t="Blackfathom Deeps can be found at the north end of Zoram Strand along the coast of Ashenvale.", d=7.440, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-ab572ddf", h="ab572ddf", t="The monastery was once a center for learning and enlightenment. With the rise of the undead Scourge during the Third War, the peaceful Monastery was converted into a stronghold of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. The Crusaders are intolerant of all non-human races, regardless of alliance or affiliation. They believe that any and all outsiders are potential carriers of the undead plague - and must be destroyed.  ", d=27.150, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-ad5ec0ca", h="ad5ec0ca", t="No, I'm not, but lots of others are looking for love.  You should buy my love tokens, put on some cologne or perfume, and then pass them around!", d=9.480, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-adc7501c", h="adc7501c", t="The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.", d=7.520, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-b63e4e81", h="b63e4e81", t="Fill yer tankard and pull up a chair. We've stories to tell and kegs to empty.", d=6.160, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-b69e98a5", h="b69e98a5", t="If you put on cologne or perfume, then you'll see who is amorous.  Those are the ones who accept love tokens... and offer a gift in return.$B$BBut remember: to give someone a love token, you have to smell just right!  Men like the scent of perfume, while women prefer cologne.", d=17.600, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-b852ea17", h="b852ea17", t="Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm's fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade's existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council.  ", d=31.630, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-b8eefffb", h="b8eefffb", t="Shadowfang Keep is in southern Silverpine just north of Pyrewood Village.", d=4.720, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-b8ef9c65", h="b8ef9c65", t="The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.", d=4.400, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-c2bfa0cf", h="c2bfa0cf", t="Gnomeregan can be found in western Dun Morogh.", d=4.000, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-ca5fde90", h="ca5fde90", t="Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.", d=6.000, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-d352a290", h="d352a290", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook. ", d=26.630, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-e99614f5", h="e99614f5", t="The ruins of Zul'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.", d=5.560, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-f106f818", h="f106f818", t="Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara's most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres.  ", d=30.070, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-f2218c4a", h="f2218c4a", t="Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.", d=6.560, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-f88f28f5", h="f88f28f5", t="Ragefire Chasm can be found beneath the Shadow Cleft in the center of Orgrimmar.", d=5.240, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
		{ f="7744-f9fa0d11", h="f9fa0d11", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Cairne, Sylvanas and Thrall.", d=17.360, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
	},
	[7763] = {
		{ f="7763-a98d4d07", h="a98d4d07", t="The Gordunni are a large ogre tribe that has control over considerable portions of forests in Feralas. Their dark magic seeps into the elements around them, damaging both the environment and the creatures that inhabit it.$B$BIf you do decide to travel to Feralas, please be mindful of these ogres -- they are quite nasty and many are able to wield powerful dark magic. ", d=18.069, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="7763-c0aa2071", h="c0aa2071", t="In a place called Feralas to the west of here, the hippogryphs, long-time companions of the night elves, are in danger.$B$BI need you to rescue an egg from the ruins of Isildien, to the south, there. The Super Egg-O-Matic can analyze any egg brought to it and judge if it is likely to hatch. I then send the eggs along to the druids, safe from the Gordunni ogres' dark magics.$B$BPlease know, $n, some of the rescued eggs are bad eggs, and will never hatch.", d=20.978, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="7763-d059fc6f", h="d059fc6f", t="Hi there! I have a proposition for an adventure-seeker such as you, if you are up to the challenge!$B$BAlong with my invention, the Super Egg-O-Matic, I am hard at work aiding the druids with their campaign to save the hippogryphs. The birds are being affected by the evil effects of the Gordunni ogres inhabiting the ruins of Feralas, and their numbers are dwindling.$B$BI collect many different types of eggs.  Will you help and find some for me?", d=19.133, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
	},
	[7766] = {
		{ f="7766-2849f8e9", h="2849f8e9", t="You'll have to be patient with me, $N. I've got my Spybot inside working on a very delicate matter. I'll be with ya in a second.  Oh, and do me a favor, try not to let Lescovar see you... we're about to ambush him.", d=11.460, v="gnome-male-standard" },
		{ f="7766-e0ee2668", h="e0ee2668", t="Oh, if I only had a tree branch to hold up in front of me. The guards would never see me then.", d=4.496, v="gnome-male-standard" },
	},
	[7771] = {
		{ f="7771-3e8d556f", h="3e8d556f", t="I know, I know, I'm out here in the middle of nowhere!$B$BMy home is actually in Ratchet, but after crashing my zeppelin here, I thought I might as well start the research I came here to do!", d=10.536, v="goblin-male-zany" },
	},
	[7772] = {
		{ f="7772-35774c27", h="35774c27", t="To get down safely, I provide wings to those in need. ", d=4.280, v="nightelf-male-official" },
	},
	[7773] = {
		{ f="7773-a32c70eb", h="a32c70eb", t="The land of Feralas has been through much, $r. The earth, the trees, the creatures; they are all changing what Feralas is and will be.$B$BThe Twin Colossals above us remain as a constant, though, throughout all that has happened here...", d=16.434, v="nightelf-female-sentinel" },
	},
	[7775] = {
		{ f="7775-0377307a", h="0377307a", t="Hi there! The name's Gregan. What can I do for ya?", d=5.080, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
		{ f="7775-664b7086", h="664b7086", t="Heh, heh... Quite the inquisitive one, aren't ya, $n? Well, here's what you need to do.$B$BNorth of here, in the old ruins, lives a very disagreeable gnoll by the name of Miblon Snarltooth. He guards the only Evoroot I know of, but he watches it night and day! Seems like he never even sleeps!$B$BWhat you can do, is bribe him. I can sell you some bait that he'll find tasty -- just put it down near him and that will distract him long enough for you to grab the Evoroot. Good luck!", d=33.550, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
		{ f="7775-c718aa29", h="c718aa29", t="Sure thing, $n. You look like you can be trusted... Trustworthy! I can spot that a mile away...$B$BAnyway, back to what I was sayin'. Takes one Evoroot plant to make the Videre Elixir. The rest 'a the ingredients are trivial really, but the Evoroot, well, that can be a bit tricky to get.", d=21.160, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
	},
	[7776] = {
		{ f="7776-af177c3f", h="af177c3f", t="Listen to the stories of an elder. $n. I have many to speak of...", d=5.820, v="tauren-male-warrior" },
	},
	[7783] = {
		{ f="7783-4ef8d7d2", h="4ef8d7d2", t="Their minds are now tainted, $r. Yes, even more so than before. They live only to serve and protect Razelikh. The amulet fragments they each hold are the key to summoning the demon lord. What you do not understand is that none of them can be harmed through any conventional means.", d=20.202, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="7783-648388c7", h="648388c7", t="Can you see them, mortal? No... I did not think you could. Sighted but sightless - it is your gift and your curse.", d=10.869, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="7783-668ad231", h="668ad231", t="In the age of war, Razelikh the Defiler served as the most fearsome of Lord Kazzak's lieutenants. When the Legion was defeated and Kazzak forced back into the Tainted Scar, Razelikh was tasked by his master to secure the Blasted Lands.$B$BWhile the Alliance fought petty battles with the Horde over territory outside of the Blasted Lands, Razelikh was uniting the differing Shadow Council sects and the brutish Dreadmaul ogres of the land.", d=31.424, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="7783-9f2406cf", h="9f2406cf", t="Then let us pretend that you undergo the long and arduous task of creating the bane necessary to break through the demonic wards placed upon the triad. What would be your next course of action? To face the Defiler in his lair?$B$B<Loramus laughs.> ", d=16.727, v="nightelf-male-warrior", P={ { d=17.616 }, { d=1.560, n=true } }, nP={ [1]={ [2]=1.880 } } },
		{ f="7783-d0061b47", h="d0061b47", t="What Sevine, Allistarj, and Grol did not realize was that just as their servants were bound to the land, so would they be... You see, the price for their own immortality was also imprisonment and eternal servitude under the command of Razelikh. The cruel cunning of Razelikh had emerged the victor once again. ", d=21.162, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="7783-e5f28cf5", h="e5f28cf5", t="Tragically, it was Thrall's wisdom that finally sealed the bond between the demon lord and his minions. It was Trebor's regiment that served as the catalyst to unite the demon lord, the shadowsworn sects and the ogres. The lure of nearly unlimited power and the granting of immortal shock troops to each respective leader sealed the deal in blood. ", d=27.142, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
	},
	[7804] = {
		{ f="7804-5b9a1535", h="5b9a1535", t="Split in two to form the one. The twin blades are bound to Zul'Farrak.$B$BSul'thraze reborn when the twins are found.", d=9.536, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="7804-b6dff793", h="b6dff793", t="Sul'thraze... the first time I heard the word uttered I was around your age. It meant nothing to me then, as it means nothing to you now. It was not until a warband of trolls coming from Zul'Farrak laid waste to the land that I understood... and feared.$B$BMany will tell you that the Splitblade of Suffering does not exist. That it's a myth; a rumor started to scare children 'straight.' But believe me, $r, it exists.$B$B<Trenton loses focus as he runs his hand across the jagged scar on his face.>", d=33.687, v="nightelf-male-warrior", P={ { d=35.950 }, { d=5.000, n=true } }, nP={ [1]={ [2]=6.320 } } },
	},
	[7823] = {
		{ f="7823-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.473, v="dwarf-female-guard" },
	},
	[7824] = {
		{ f="7824-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.661, v="orc-male-standard" },
	},
	[7852] = {
		{ f="7852-0446078d", h="0446078d", t="Greetings $c -- if you're looking for leather goods and leatherworking supplies, you've come to the right semi-retired Paladin.", d=8.900, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="7852-d1e7a110", h="d1e7a110", t="I swear... if Quint tries to plant one more fishing grub on me, I'm going to hack down his tree with my not-so-rusty sword.", d=9.329, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[7853] = {
		{ f="7853-967b8e4a", h="967b8e4a", t="Hello, $N! I am master engineer, Scooty.", d=4.344, v="goblin-male-zany" },
	},
	[7854] = {
		{ f="7854-c41fd9a4", h="c41fd9a4", t="Welcome to Camp Mojache, brave $c.  How may I assist you this day?", d=7.080, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[7866] = {
		{ f="7866-6d31ac42", h="6d31ac42", t="If you are here to hunt dragons, be my guest.  Where should I send my condolences?", d=5.491, v="human-male-official" },
	},
	[7867] = {
		{ f="7867-e1ab764e", h="e1ab764e", t="Your stench will attract every dragon for miles.  Tell me what you want, and quickly.", d=8.200, v="orc-male-guard" },
	},
	[7868] = {
		{ f="7868-8fbbd43c", h="8fbbd43c", t="Oh hi! My name's Sarah. What can I do for you?", d=4.400, v="human-female-warrior" },
	},
	[7869] = {
		{ f="7869-571feb74", h="571feb74", t="The spirits told me you would come, that you would seek me for some reason, but that even you may not know that reason. So, do you know why you are here?", d=13.520, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[7870] = {
		{ f="7870-975c76d8", h="975c76d8", t="The forest told me of your presence, but not why you were here. So, speak and enlighten me.", d=7.092, v="nightelf-female-sentinel" },
	},
	[7871] = {
		{ f="7871-649568e4", h="649568e4", t="How you doin' mon!", d=1.680, v="troll-male-shaman" },
	},
	[7875] = {
		{ f="7875-801c29a1", h="801c29a1", t="We must ensure the survival of this camp at all costs, $c!  Our enemies must not be given any quarter, for they would surely give us none were we to need it.", d=9.919, v="tauren-male-warrior" },
	},
	[7879] = {
		{ f="7879-adbf2a6a", h="adbf2a6a", t="Greetings, $c.  What may this humble servant of the Feathermoon Stronghold do for you today?", d=8.440, v="nightelf-male-official" },
	},
	[7916] = {
		{ f="7916-2e7ff92c", h="2e7ff92c", t="Hello, $n. I train and care for young hippogryphs here; feel free to have a look around.", d=8.081, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="7916-304ccce3", h="304ccce3", t="Druids are very sensitive to the plight of all creatures of the world. When it was found that these birds were in danger, we set up a system of rescuing them from the corruption of Feralas.$B$BA gnome named Curgle Cranklehop leads the affair; she collects the eggs and has them sent here, where I care for them.$B$BWe could always use more help for our cause, $n. Maybe you should head over to Gadgetzan and look for Curgle.", d=30.212, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
	},
	[7918] = {
		{ f="7918-1798ee16", h="1798ee16", t="Uldum is a research facility for the Creators in their continuing efforts to enhance the biosphere of Azeroth.  Specific information regarding their work as it relates to Uldum is restricted to those individuals who possess the Plates of Uldum in their disc sets.$B$BData repositories inside the Uldum complex have been programmed to address specific experiments and data compilations; please refer to them for detailed information.", d=27.413, v="human-male" },
		{ f="7918-6ca96c61", h="6ca96c61", t="Several sets of the Plates of Uldum have been synthesized by the Creators for their expressed use.  The Creators control the distribution of said discs for all complexes on this world.  As such, Azeroth has been rescheduled for visitation, and therefore future discs may enter circulation at that time.$B$BExisting discs have been fully distributed to those parties with appropriate security clearance.", d=25.791, v="human-male" },
		{ f="7918-8da060df", h="8da060df", t="The Plates of Uldum are discs synthesized by the Creators that allow access into the Uldum compound.  These discs house and store specific data related to the Creators' activities here.$B$BPhysically, they are nearly identical in circumference to the disc set you currently possess.  Their markings, however, are directly related to information on Uldum as opposed to the Uldaman complex.", d=26.500, v="human-male" },
		{ f="7918-b4f0525b", h="b4f0525b", t="Salutations.  I am a guardian of entry.  Unless you have the Plates of Uldum already integrated with your disc set, I will not allow for entry into the Uldum compound.", d=11.495, v="human-male" },
		{ f="7918-b7d236ab", h="b7d236ab", t="The Creators use visitation as a means to reestablish control over seeded worlds when forces, both external and internal, upset the matrix dynamics associated with it.  Such tactics are not to be taken lightly when executed by the Creators.$B$BFor additional information on this world's scheduled visitation, please consult the appropriate data repository that fields all Creator-related scheduling considerations.", d=28.827, v="human-male" },
		{ f="7918-cf4fcf43", h="cf4fcf43", t="My purpose is to regulate access to the Uldum complex for the Creators.  I allow entry into the compound only when the solicitor exhibits for access the proper sequencing discs.$B$BYour disc set currently does not contain the Plates of Uldum, the primary prerequisite for entry.  Access is not granted unless the Plates of Uldum are present.", d=24.800, v="human-male" },
	},
	[7937] = {
		{ f="7937-51417c16", h="51417c16", t="Hello there, $c. I am High Tinker Mekkatorque of the exiles of Gnomeregan.", d=7.120, v="npc-7006" },
		{ f="7937-825d4590", h="825d4590", t="Oh yes, how wonderful! I have been expecting an emissary from your people, and I am very happy to make your acquaintance.    I do wish I could receive you in our home city of Gnomeregan, but our people have recently fallen on hard times and our homeland is, at present, lost to us.    King Bronzebeard is ever a friend to us gnomes, however, and has graciously opened his city to us in this difficult time.     I hope that your adventures on Azeroth treat you well, and I look forward to further opportunities to learn more of your people.     Farewell, $N.", d=39.310, v="npc-7006" },
		{ f="7937-98814444", h="98814444", t="Oh yes, how wonderful! I have been expecting an emissary from your people, and I am very happy to make your acquaintance.    I do wish I could receive you in our home city of Gnomeregan, but our people have recently fallen on hard times and our homeland is, at present, lost to us.    King Bronzebeard is ever a friend to we gnomes however, and has graciously opened his city to us in this difficult time.     I hope that your adventures on Azeroth treat you well, and I look forward to further opportunities to learn more of your people.     Farewell, $N.", d=39.990, v="npc-7006" },
	},
	[7944] = {
		{ f="7944-5a81ed46", h="5a81ed46", t="Greetings!  If you are here to access gnome engineering schemata, please have your gnome engineer membership card ready for verification.", d=6.934, v="gnome-male-standard" },
		{ f="7944-9a62fac1", h="9a62fac1", t="I am Tinkmaster Overspark, and I am the chief architect for modern gnomish engineering principles in the world today.  It is my job to ensure that the power of invention continues to shine brightest from our arclight spanners than anywhere else!  Also, if you happen to know a good schematic for radiation elimination, we just so happen to be in the market for one right about now...", d=17.535, v="gnome-male-standard" },
	},
	[7948] = {
		{ f="7948-24316ec5", h="24316ec5", t="Have you come here for instruction in the art of making potions? You were mistaken if you thought that I would offer such a privilege to you, unearned. Go, and do not return to me until you have greater skill.", d=16.960, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
		{ f="7948-64f3e401", h="64f3e401", t="Once I welcomed darkness, for it was the sister of night. Now it is dark all the time, even during the day, and the forests cry out for sustenance. Unless we act soon, this spreading blight will cover the world.", d=16.240, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
		{ f="7948-aadb15af", h="aadb15af", t="Your skill displays an enduring affection for our art, but I would see further evidence of your commitment. I shall charge you with a task. Fulfill it, and I will be content.", d=14.200, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
	},
	[7949] = {
		{ f="7949-465e9d4b", h="465e9d4b", t="I know many things, stranger, but your knowledge rivals my own. Enchanters who wish to hone their skills further are known to travel to the Tower of Azora, where an artisan named Kitta Firewind resides.", d=15.600, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
		{ f="7949-a0f54803", h="a0f54803", t="Why don't we see just what you're capable of? If you complete the task I shall be happy to further your training! ", d=7.840, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
		{ f="7949-c3e89db3", h="c3e89db3", t="If you are seeking a truly rewarding pursuit, then a life of enchanting is for you!", d=8.280, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
	},
	[7951] = {
		{ f="7951-e0a94ace", h="e0a94ace", t="Hail $c. Didn't I see you recently at an exclusive gathering? You look familiar, but then again this city is a busy place.$B$BIf you attended that convention, then surely you were given a secret code. Tell me your code and I will give you a special prize in return.", d=19.640, v="orc-male-shady" },
	},
	[7952] = {
		{ f="7952-17d55d66", h="17d55d66", t="I'm sorry $g mon : sis;, but I won't be sellin' my raptors to someone who hasn't proven themselves to be exalted to the Darkspear tribe.  When ya make a stand and show yourself to be no less than exalted to us, then I'll make my raptors available to ya.", d=18.560, v="troll-male-dark", g=true },
		{ f="7952-fcb64345", h="fcb64345", t="And a good day to ya, brave $c.  I know ya be lookin' for a fine steed.  There's no finer steed than a raptor under your reigns, lemme tell you $g mon : sis;!  Take a look at the ones I got to offer - bred from the fiercest stock anywhere.", d=20.280, v="troll-male-dark", g=true },
	},
	[7953] = {
		{ f="7953-088823f1", h="088823f1", t="Ey, friend! I be happy to offer you a riding raptor, but first you should be trainin' with Xar'Ti.    These fearless creatures aren't easily ridden, but once ya know how to ride one you will not find a better companion. Mind the claws though, just one swipe can take down a fully grown kodo.", d=25.680, v="troll-female-standard" },
		{ f="7953-6d4ea044", h="6d4ea044", t="I cannot be teachin' a Tauren to ride a Raptor.", d=4.080, v="troll-female-standard" },
		{ f="7953-a3eec9a8", h="a3eec9a8", t="You need to be exalted with the trolls of the Darkspear tribe before I will teach you a riding skill, $c.", d=11.320, v="troll-female-standard" },
		{ f="7953-de02093f", h="de02093f", t="I can teach you the finer points of Raptor Riding, provided you have enough gold to cover the lesson!", d=10.760, v="troll-female-standard" },
	},
	[7954] = {
		{ f="7954-0343a5f9", h="0343a5f9", t="I'd be wasting both your gold and my time if I were to teach you how to pilot a Mechanostrider, $c.  You're just too large!", d=6.102, v="gnome-male-zany" },
		{ f="7954-471341e8", h="471341e8", t="I can teach you the finer points of Mechanostrider Piloting, provided you have enough gold to cover the lesson!", d=4.832, v="gnome-male-zany" },
		{ f="7954-fd743840", h="fd743840", t="You need to be exalted with the gnomes of the Gnomeregan Exiles before I will teach you how to pilot a Mechanostrider, $c.", d=7.378, v="gnome-male-zany" },
	},
	[7955] = {
		{ f="7955-262c603f", h="262c603f", t="Um... I think you're a little too big to ride a Mechano-strider there, $g mister : ma'am;.  You'd likely crush the finely tuned servo-balancers!", d=6.356, v="gnome-female-nerdy", g=true },
		{ f="7955-42fb1f5a", h="42fb1f5a", t="If you have come looking for the gift of fast and safe mobility, then you have arrived at your destination!  This year's model of the new Mechano-striders have recently arrived, and I am ready to show you all they have to offer!", d=10.346, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="7955-53cc47ec", h="53cc47ec", t="Erm... I really don't know you that well, sorry.  I mean, as an authorized Mechanostrider dealer, I really only can sell my mounts to those people who are considered exalted amongst the gnomes.  If you ever are recognized as exalted to Gnomeregan, I'd be happy to show you what I have to offer.", d=12.877, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="7955-84efac38", h="84efac38", t="Salutations, friend! I would be happy to offer you a Mechanostrider, but first you should train with my brother Binjy, over there.    They are far more reliable than any beast but can be difficult to pilot for a first time rider, but once you know how to pilot one you will not find a better companion!", d=12.806, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
	},
	[7999] = {
		{ f="7999-3d397bbf", h="3d397bbf", t="Greetings, $c. I am Tyrande Whisperwind, High Priestess of Elune.", d=6.320, v="npc-7274" },
		{ f="7999-ccf70497", h="ccf70497", t="It pleases me greatly to at last meet one of your people. I've heard much of the shen'dorei and your long history, and I am glad to see our cousins return home to Kalimdor at long last.    I confess that our people have a... complicated relationship with the highborne. Some amongst the night elves are quick to distrust those of highborne descent such as those in your High Order. However, you have my assurance that you will be shown the utmost respect while a guest in our city.    Please, make yourself at home here. I'd encourage you to explore and familiarize yourself with our culture. It is, after all, your culture as well in a way.", d=45.940, v="npc-7274" },
	},
	[8018] = {
		{ f="8018-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=1.920, v="dwarf-male-standard" },
	},
	[8019] = {
		{ f="8019-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.280, v="nightelf-male-standard" },
	},
	[8020] = {
		{ f="8020-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.630, v="tauren-female-official" },
	},
	[8115] = {
		{ f="8115-1330f3e3", h="1330f3e3", t="Incredible power can be found in the spirits or \"muisek\" of the creatures that we battle against.$B$BLook inside yourself; learn to harness the power of your own spirit, and you will be more powerful than you ever imagined.", d=13.760, v="troll-male-shaman" },
		{ f="8115-9733bd67", h="9733bd67", t="Existing in this area are many creatures considered allies of the night elves. The elves have had access to the power within each of these creatures; it is time that the horde be allowed this same satisfaction. I have devised a way that this power can be captured and used for our benefit.$B$BDo not doubt what I tell you, $n. Help me, and you shall see that I speak truth.", d=26.070, v="troll-male-shaman" },
	},
	[8125] = {
		{ f="8125-bfc13a0b", h="bfc13a0b", t="We may have been suffering a drought but there's no shortage of meat! Care to browse my goods?", d=5.906, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[8126] = {
		{ f="8126-8b85068d", h="8b85068d", t="Let me break down a little math for you: \"goblin\" plus \"engineering\" equals KNOW HOW, baby.  Anyone who tells you otherwise simply doesn't know how to add.", d=11.278, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
		{ f="8126-f3c8f530", h="f3c8f530", t="Greetings!  If you are here to access goblin engineering schemata, please have your goblin engineer membership card ready for verification.", d=10.213, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[8140] = {
		{ f="8140-08830bac", h="08830bac", t="Through rigorous retraining I have had to break many students of all they had previously learned so that I might teach them anew.  The service I offer becomes increasingly difficult to perform each time it is done.  It is for that reason that it becomes increasingly expensive with each retraining.  Do you desire that I break you of the talents you have learned?", d=22.091, v="human-male-warrior" },
		{ f="8140-837f02f9", h="837f02f9", t="May the Light protect you this day.", d=2.303, v="human-male-warrior" },
	},
	[8141] = {
		{ f="8141-08830bac", h="08830bac", t="Through rigorous retraining I have had to break many students of all they had previously learned so that I might teach them anew.  The service I offer becomes increasingly difficult to perform each time it is done.  It is for that reason that it becomes increasingly expensive with each retraining.  Do you desire that I break you of the talents you have learned?", d=22.455, v="human-male-warrior" },
		{ f="8141-57c322c3", h="57c322c3", t="While Theramore is reknown for it's exceptional training of warriors, I am afraid that I can not help you.", d=8.081, v="human-male-warrior" },
		{ f="8141-a1ab53e2", h="a1ab53e2", t="Come to train with the Theramore guard have you?", d=3.152, v="human-male-warrior" },
	},
	[8142] = {
		{ f="8142-08830bac", h="08830bac", t="Through rigorous retraining I have had to break many students of all they had previously learned so that I might teach them anew.  The service I offer becomes increasingly difficult to perform each time it is done.  It is for that reason that it becomes increasingly expensive with each retraining.  Do you desire that I break you of the talents you have learned?", d=26.510, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="8142-7b785024", h="7b785024", t="Many are the paths of the Earth Mother.  May your ancestors watch over you $c.", d=7.640, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="8142-d1e27715", h="d1e27715", t="$n, how may I further your training in the eyes of the Earth Mother?", d=6.000, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[8153] = {
		{ f="8153-61b74186", h="61b74186", t="The strongest hides come from those kodo that have laid themselves to rest in this wasteland.", d=7.400, v="tauren-male-elder" },
	},
	[8306] = {
		{ f="8306-0c543544", h="0c543544", t="Cooking is a life long pursuit and I see we share the same passion!", d=5.360, v="orc-male-shady" },
		{ f="8306-3b48d638", h="3b48d638", t="Dirge Quikcleave of Gadgetzan is a master of the culinary arts.  To better yourself you will need to seek him out.", d=9.720, v="orc-male-shady" },
		{ f="8306-48c1c064", h="48c1c064", t="Wulan in Shadowprey Village can sell you the \"Expert Cookbook\".  You will need that if you are to better yourself.", d=9.840, v="orc-male-shady" },
		{ f="8306-b48f927f", h="b48f927f", t="I can teach you how to cook!", d=2.520, v="orc-male-shady" },
	},
	[8308] = {
		{ f="8308-08830bac", h="08830bac", t="Through rigorous retraining I have had to break many students of all they had previously learned so that I might teach them anew.  The service I offer becomes increasingly difficult to perform each time it is done.  It is for that reason that it becomes increasingly expensive with each retraining.  Do you desire that I break you of the talents you have learned?", d=24.273, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="8308-3a9ead82", h="3a9ead82", t="I train hunters in the ways and traditions of our ancestors.", d=4.404, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="8308-c8a70fb5", h="c8a70fb5", t="What can I do for you my child?", d=2.626, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
		{ f="8308-f9b860f0", h="f9b860f0", t="I cannot train a $c such as yourself.", d=4.566, v="nightelf-male-warrior" },
	},
	[8359] = {
		{ f="8359-6fec0ef7", h="6fec0ef7", t="Greetings.  If you are here for leather goods, then you will find my wares well crafted.", d=6.560, v="tauren-male-shaman" },
	},
	[8380] = {
		{ f="8380-3bb3e214", h="3bb3e214", t="Ahoy, $n! Not a pretty picture, is it?$B$BThe Horizon Scout at the bottom of the sea, my crew in shambles, and our cargo and passengers strewn about like so much debris that you'd think this was one of Stormwind's canals after a festival.$B$BAnd that's not where the trouble ends...", d=15.720, v="human-female-warrior" },
		{ f="8380-9520ba66", h="9520ba66", t="You'll have to give me a moment, $c, the naga are attacking us right now. I'll speak to you as soon as the attack is done!", d=6.160, v="human-female-warrior" },
	},
	[8399] = {
		{ f="8399-11ac90fa", h="11ac90fa", t="Greetings, $Gsir:miss;. I am Master Xylem's apprentice Nyrill. If you have any concerns, please feel free to bring them up with the master.$B$BI will be here to serve you when you're ready to return down to the base of the mountain.", d=14.865, v="human-male-standard", g=true },
	},
	[8403] = {
		{ f="8403-2020ffb8", h="2020ffb8", t="Wanna buy a cockroach?", d=1.520, v="scourge-male-dark" },
	},
	[8436] = {
		{ f="8436-2d917e3d", h="2d917e3d", t="Praise Elune! It has been many years since I have had visitors.", d=6.120, v="nightelf-male-official" },
		{ f="8436-e83ffdfb", h="e83ffdfb", t="Etched into a tablet of pure gold was the embodiment of my remorse, shame, regret, and sorrow. Unfortunately, the Twilight's Hammer found the tablet and branded me a blasphemer. I was summarily executed, my prayer to Elune incomplete. I am now bound to this world as a spirit, unable to transcend to the Nether; held in this cage as a warning to all that would betray the faith of the Twilight's Hammer. ", d=32.190, v="nightelf-male-official" },
		{ f="8436-f7b13c50", h="f7b13c50", t="As a young night elf in Darkshore, I crossed paths with a group of unsavory individuals known as the Twilight's Hammer. A group of them befriended me and shamefully, I ended up eschewing my faith in Elune and embracing the vitriol of the Twilight's Hammer.$B$BIt was not until a vision came to me from Elune, that I woke up from the malaise that I had fallen into as a follower of the old gods.$B$BIn repentance, I began work on my prayer to Elune. ", d=32.870, v="nightelf-male-official" },
	},
	[8441] = {
		{ f="8441-6ca49819", h="6ca49819", t="What want from Raze??", d=1.320, v="narrator", n={ [1]=2.320 } },
	},
	[8479] = {
		{ f="8479-0624fb39", h="0624fb39", t="As you can see, I am but one man with a lumbering oaf of a squire. The might of the Dark Iron dwarves and the beasts held in the grip of Ragnaros would surely overwhelm me alone, but I have the utmost confidence that such a brave and ambitious adventurer such as you would have no problem handling the denizens of the cauldron. Should you choose to assist me, I shall reward you with riches and wealth beyond your wildest dreams.", d=26.894, v="human-male-official" },
		{ f="8479-78f5350d", h="78f5350d", t="My father was slain by the filth that inhabits the cauldron. My pleas for assistance to the Stormwind magistrate fell on deaf ears. Nay, they want not to admit that this part of the world even exists, let alone send their precious military in to administer justice.$B$BI seek vengeance, $r, plain and simple. Is there a more passionate cause in this world?", d=23.082, v="human-male-official" },
		{ f="8479-d1030815", h="d1030815", t="Vengeance shall be mine.", d=2.410, v="human-male-official" },
	},
	[8496] = {
		{ f="8496-26f5ad55", h="26f5ad55", t="Hi there. No, Marvon sure isn't here, and he won't be back for quite some time. Actually, I am getting a little worried about him...$B$BI hope he gets back soon. A large chest arrived for him and it's too heavy for me to lug it inside here! I had to leave it out by the door...", d=18.800, v="goblin-female-s107" },
		{ f="8496-944c29ff", h="944c29ff", t="Hiya! This workshop isn't mine, no! But one day after I finish training I am going to be an inventor, just like my hero, Marvon Rivetseeker.  You've never heard of him? Well it just so happens that he left quite some time ago to study some ancient troll ruins he kept talking about. He left in a zeppelin... not quite sure about where exactly he went...  Tanarasin? Tenkeris? Taneranisany?  <Liv shakes her head.>  No, that's not it...", d=27.950, v="goblin-female-s107", P={ { d=27.310 }, { d=3.000, n=true }, { d=2.600 } }, nP={ [1]={ [2]=2.200 } } },
	},
	[8508] = {
		{ f="8508-15b608c8", h="15b608c8", t="Lookin' to fish? Then you'll need the proper tools.", d=2.800, v="dwarf-female-young", s={ ["m"]=3.040 } },
	},
	[8509] = {
		{ f="8509-3c6d1295", h="3c6d1295", t="I live only to serve the master.", d=2.990, v="human-male-warrior" },
	},
	[8576] = {
		{ f="8576-d21575bc", h="d21575bc", t="The days we've spent here in Azshara are not among our best and most glorious, but we are still young and blood still courses through our veins--we shall find victory here. It is only a matter of time.", d=16.640, v="orc-male-guard" },
	},
	[8579] = {
		{ f="8579-0d76e20b", h="0d76e20b", t="Greetings, $c.  Though time and drink have dulled my outer senses, my inner eyes remain strong.", d=7.880, v="troll-male-shaman" },
		{ f="8579-161a09e4", h="161a09e4", t="Through my studies, I see that defeating the god Hakkar's avatar has weakened him.  But the bulk of his strength remains, lurking at the far end of the Nether.$B$BYou have defeated his avatar once, $n.  Perhaps if you defeat it again you can further weaken the god so that, one day, we might face his true self.$B$BI have prepared a spell that you may use to again summon an avatar of Hakkar within the Sanctum of the Fallen God.  Do you want to confront it once again?", d=31.590, v="troll-male-shaman" },
	},
	[8587] = {
		{ f="8587-8b1070f2", h="8b1070f2", t="I am not here because of honor, $n. I am here because of one orc's pride.$B$BIf I had not rejected Belgrom's offers, then I'm sure I'd still be in Orgrimmar taking care of real business.$B$BHis desire for women is not unknown to many of the female warriors in Durotar, but that doesn't stop him from being his charming self.$B$BHe's lucky he didn't pursue his desire for me much longer though--he'd be short more than just the digits on his hands.", d=29.310, v="orc-female-warrior" },
	},
	[8609] = {
		{ f="8609-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.200, v="human-female-official" },
	},
	[8610] = {
		{ f="8610-c5ceacbe", h="c5ceacbe", t="Where would you like to fly to?", d=2.257, v="orc-male-standard" },
	},
	[8659] = {
		{ f="8659-b2489254", h="b2489254", t="I give you warm greetin's, $c, as does the Shattered Hand.$B$BDo not look so surprised, $n. There be shadows even on the highest perches of Orgrimmar--somethin' must hide there. The Shattered Hand take that role willingly. Thrall, even in his good heart, acknowledge that the Hand be necessary to ensure orc and troll safety.$B$BBut you not here to talk 'bout my business, you here for somethin' else.", d=36.910, v="troll-male-dark" },
		{ f="8659-f590cabf", h="f590cabf", t="Un'Goro Crater be far to the south of Kalimdor. Beyond the Thousand Needles in Tanaris. Look for the large floating stones... they mark the entrance to the Crater. But be careful... it is no easy path. The raptors are not far from the entrance.", d=22.160, v="troll-male-dark" },
	},
	[8696] = {
		{ f="8696-00934874", h="00934874", t="Thank you for saving me!$B$BI'm a cook and an alchemist from Stormwind.  I was here looking for local herbs and recipes for my uncle Angus when these quilboar captured me.  If you hadn't come around, I'm sure I'd have ended up in their stew pot!", d=13.760, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="8696-78f9fe28", h="78f9fe28", t="Hm... yes, I do have a recipe you might find useful.  Let me teach you!", d=5.982, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="8696-7bce189d", h="7bce189d", t="Your talents in cooking are a little too low.  Maybe with some practice I can teach you what I know.", d=6.427, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="8696-8ae399e4", h="8ae399e4", t="Well yes, I do know a rare alchemical recipe.  Let me teach you!", d=5.446, v="human-male-standard" },
		{ f="8696-eb17d15b", h="eb17d15b", t="Your skills in alchemy aren't yet high enough to benefit from my teachings.  Perhaps if you speak with me later...", d=6.995, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[8736] = {
		{ f="8736-54a80154", h="54a80154", t="I would never turn away someone who's ready to train with me. Unfortunately, you're not! You've still got a ways to go kid!", d=7.300, v="goblin-male-zany" },
		{ f="8736-92efd66e", h="92efd66e", t="I've been working on a way to transport oil underground between major cities, but everyone tells me it's a pipe dream.", d=6.244, v="goblin-male-zany" },
		{ f="8736-c9966b86", h="c9966b86", t="Show me what you got! You won't be sorry, I promise!", d=3.309, v="goblin-male-zany" },
	},
	[8737] = {
		{ f="8737-0479ad61", h="0479ad61", t="I... I'm not really sure how I got here...$B$BI seem to remember traveling... a raft...$B$B", d=3.839, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="8737-3dde1bdf", h="3dde1bdf", t="Pay me and I'll talk...$B$BOh hey, it's you, $n! Nevermind about that...", d=4.070, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="8737-53d35916", h="53d35916", t="Does my name sound familiar to you? Maybe we knew each other a long time ago...$B$BI think I'm named after someone important...", d=5.632, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="8737-8e3978ce", h="8e3978ce", t="Hi there! I'm glad you came back, $n. Tell me, have you completed the first quest I gave you? If you have, I might have a second quest for you...", d=6.661, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="8737-9699cf40", h="9699cf40", t="When I was wandering the crater after I crashed here, I remembered something that I once was told... \"Go up, up the mountain ahead,\" said the voice in my head.$B$BListening to it is how I ended up here, $n!", d=8.906, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="8737-9a3bc9b2", h="9a3bc9b2", t="It's a secret to everybody... including me!$B$BI'm glad you found me -- it's a good thing I'm not hiding in a bush or underneath a rock, isn't it?", d=6.883, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="8737-c58826d3", h="c58826d3", t="A long time ago, during my travels, I met a man that told me, \"Master using it and you can have this.\"$B$BWhat do you suppose that means? I didn't know then, and I still don't now, really...", d=8.443, v="gnome-male-young" },
	},
	[8738] = {
		{ f="8738-f3c8f530", h="f3c8f530", t="Greetings!  If you are here to access goblin engineering schemata, please have your goblin engineer membership card ready for verification.", d=9.720, v="goblin-male-gruff" },
	},
	[8767] = {
		{ f="8767-5fe82366", h="5fe82366", t="Thank you, little $r!", d=2.600, v="ogre-male" },
	},
	[8816] = {
		{ f="8816-3a1a50a2", h="3a1a50a2", t="I am bound eternally to this cursed world. What is it you desire, mortal?", d=5.440, v="narrator", n={ [1]=6.440 } },
		{ f="8816-e2ce2c7c", h="e2ce2c7c", t="If it is your desire to visit the rise of the Defiler, you have only to ask. I am able to transport you and your comrades.", d=8.120, v="narrator", n={ [1]=10.000 } },
	},
	[8879] = {
		{ f="8879-2701a72f", h="2701a72f", t="Greetings, $n. Have you come to learn of the history of Ironforge?", d=4.083, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
		{ f="8879-5beb9b10", h="5beb9b10", t="We need adventurers to assist us, $n. Will you help?", d=3.681, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
		{ f="8879-e0ee34a3", h="e0ee34a3", t="Notify me when you are ready to listen to the story.", d=2.810, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
		{ f="8879-ea2e9af7", h="ea2e9af7", t="Recently, the Dark Irons have been seen on the surface world with greater regularity. Fortresses have been built in the Badlands. Massive exploratory forces have been sent into the depths of Uldaman in search of ancient lore. They have even invaded our own homeland, striking at our dam near the loch.", d=17.592, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
		{ f="8879-ebc8e825", h="ebc8e825", t="We do not know.$B$BThe Dark Irons that did survive made their way into the mountain and began rebuilding their city.$B$BFrom the ashes of Thaurissan then rose Blackrock Spire and the new Dark Iron nation. Additional fortifications were made within the Searing Gorge, in the area known as the Cauldron.$B$BStories of an ancient evil that controlled the kingdom of Dark Irons began to circulate. ", d=21.928, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
		{ f="8879-f390d49a", h="f390d49a", t="Hundreds of years ago, the great city of Thaurissan stood proudly in a lush expanse of land that is now the dilapidated Burning Steppes.$B$BThaurissan was home to the nation of Dark Iron dwarves and at the time, in the midst of a civil war among the dwarven nation at large.$B$BYou see, that area of the world was at one point in time part of the Redridge Mountains - until the day that Thaurissan was consumed by a gigantic explosion. The city lay in ruin, the surrounding areas reduced to an ashy wasteland. ", d=28.915, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
	},
	[8888] = {
		{ f="8888-26ebe868", h="26ebe868", t="My great hammer, Ironfel, was handed down to the new chief architect, Fineous Darkvire: A man of despicable motive and little talent.$B$BThis is where you come in, $n. I want him stopped. He is too inept to harness the true power of Ironfel, but should one come after him with the aptitude to use Ironfel to its full potential, the destruction they could cause with their creations would be disastrous to this world. ", d=25.630, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="8888-2ca32f21", h="2ca32f21", t="I stood by and watched the corruption of Ragnaros seep through the hearts and minds of the Dark Iron nation. This once honorable race, driven to madness... to evil.$B$BWhen the construction of the Spire was complete, my will to live amongst my people gave way. I passed as a hero of the new nation of Dark Iron. This tomb was placed here - at the entrance to the city I planned and built - in honor of my efforts.", d=25.270, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="8888-93dd4660", h="93dd4660", t="I had no choice, or so I thought. I would endure the destruction of Thaurissan and stand by the side of my king and his people.$B$BUnder the control of Ragnaros, King Dagran Thaurissan tore out the heart of this mountain and erected Blackrock Spire. We worked tirelessly to build a dwarven city mightier than any city or fortress that came before... or would come after.", d=24.990, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="8888-ff72e15a", h="ff72e15a", t="Greetings, $r. I am Franclorn Forgewright. Are you here to learn of the Spire and of Dark Iron?", d=6.600, v="dwarf-male" },
	},
	[8931] = {
		{ f="8931-03ca5480", h="03ca5480", t="Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.   ", d=28.310, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-174473b0", h="174473b0", t="Recently, a night elf druid named Naralex discovered a network of underground caverns within the heart of the Barrens. Believing he could use the caverns' springs to restore lushness to the Barrens, the druid began siphoning the energies of the fabled Emerald Dream. His vision somehow became a nightmare, however, and soon the Wailing Caverns changed into a den of vicious, deadly predators. It is said that Naralex still resides somewhere inside the labyrinth, trapped beyond the edges of the Emerald Dream.  ", d=35.270, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-17e9d243", h="17e9d243", t="Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world's creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone.  ", d=36.620, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-19490f29", h="19490f29", t="Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar's spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ", d=37.390, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-19cbe7de", h="19cbe7de", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Bolvar, Magni, or Tyrande.", d=19.040, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-1a6e2552", h="1a6e2552", t="This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul'Farrak's walls. ", d=30.150, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-22aa3fe4", h="22aa3fe4", t="Razorfen Downs can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the east side of the road.", d=6.680, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-29b91ff4", h="29b91ff4", t="The old Assembly of Thanes is a chamber below the great city of Ironforge, the ancestral home of the Bronzebeard clan. Its depths plunge to the deepest parts of the heart of Khaz Modan, and rumor has it immense geodes crown the chamber.", d=16.360, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-2e88eda5", h="2e88eda5", t="Frustrated by the Dalaran wizards' lack of progress against the undead during the Third War, the Archmage Arugal elected to summon the extra-dimensional worgen to bolster his side's diminishing ranks. The wolf-men slaughtered the Scourge, then quickly turned on the wizards themselves and laid siege to the keep of the noble, Baron Silverlaine. The fort quickly fell into shadow and ruin. Driven mad with guilt, Arugal adopted the worgen as his children and retreated to the newly dubbed 'Shadowfang Keep'.  ", d=34.420, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-3141b27b", h="3141b27b", t="Crafted from the same vines as Razorfen Kraul, Razorfen Downs is the traditional capital city of the quilboar race. The sprawling, thorn-ridden labyrinth houses a veritable army of loyal quilboar as well as their high priests - the Death's Head tribe. Recently, however, a looming shadow has fallen over the crude den. Agents of the undead Scourge - led by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer - have taken control over the quilboar race and turned the maze of thorns into a bastion of undead might.   ", d=36.790, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-330cd2db", h="330cd2db", t="The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves' holdings in the mountain's volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself.  ", d=31.990, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-33439fd8", h="33439fd8", t="Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal'ai's plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple's ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons. ", d=35.630, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-342c02c0", h="342c02c0", t="The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free.  ", d=27.910, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-4a0923b3", h="4a0923b3", t="Are you interested in exploring one of these dungeons?", d=3.400, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-4a6950fb", h="4a6950fb", t="The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.", d=4.640, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-4f48ef1f", h="4f48ef1f", t="Situated along the Zoram Strand of Ashenvale, Blackfathom Deeps was once a glorious temple dedicated to the night elves' moon-goddess Elune. However, the great Sundering shattered the temple - sinking it beneath the waves of the Veiled Sea. There it remained untouched - until, drawn by its ancient power - the naga and satyr emerged to plumb its secrets. Legends hold that the ancient beast, Aku'mai, has taken up residence within the temple's ruins.  ", d=30.790, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-581034a1", h="581034a1", t="The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ", d=34.310, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-5dc31760", h="5dc31760", t="During the War of the Ancients, the demigod Agamaggan came forth to battle the Burning Legion. The colossal boar was defeated, and over time in the areas where his blood fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted to life. The quilboar came to occupy these regions and hold them sacred. The heart of these massive thorn-colonies is the Razorfen. Razorfen Kraul was conquered by the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who some speculate has been negotiating with agents of the Scourge for some insidious purpose. ", d=35.150, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-5eccd4fa", h="5eccd4fa", t="The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.", d=6.160, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-5ff7a251", h="5ff7a251", t="Scarlet Monastery lies in the hills northeast of Tirisfal Glades.", d=5.920, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-66f64f6e", h="66f64f6e", t="Razorfen Kraul can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the west side of the road.", d=6.680, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-69040db4", h="69040db4", t="Love tokens are small messages of affection you can give to amorous town and city folk.  Such people will reward you with a gift of adoration.$B$BOr, if you are already adored by another, then at the least they'll give you a gift of friendship.", d=15.760, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-6a089d41", h="6a089d41", t="The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.", d=6.000, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-70185dce", h="70185dce", t="Uldaman can be found at the very northern end of the Badlands.", d=4.400, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-7b1bcef4", h="7b1bcef4", t="The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.", d=5.080, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-7de88db1", h="7de88db1", t="Located in Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan has been the gnomes' capital city for generations, though it was recently infested by mutant troggs. In a desperate attempt to retaliate, High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the emergency venting of the city's radioactive waste tanks. Though the troggs became irradiated, their siege continued unabated and the gnomes were forced to seek refuge in the dwarven city of Ironforge, where the High Tinker now enlists brave souls to help his people reclaim their beloved city.  ", d=33.550, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-864c5566", h="864c5566", t="The Wailing Caverns has its entrance at the Lushwater Oasis southwest of Crossroads in the Barrens.   ", d=6.880, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-886683cb", h="886683cb", t="The old kingdom of Lordaeron is perilous. We urge caution for anyone who dares to venture into the now decaying lands of Tirisfal Glades. If you must, find the Undercity and the upper courtyards are what you seek.", d=14.080, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-95351c86", h="95351c86", t="Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat.  ", d=34.910, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-a9b2021a", h="a9b2021a", t="The Hall of Thanes is sealed off. Those without audience to king Magni Bronzebeard must earn his trust and approval to venture into the depths of old Ironforge.", d=12.080, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-a9df0aa1", h="a9df0aa1", t="Blackfathom Deeps can be found at the north end of Zoram Strand along the coast of Ashenvale.", d=6.400, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-ab572ddf", h="ab572ddf", t="The monastery was once a center for learning and enlightenment. With the rise of the undead Scourge during the Third War, the peaceful Monastery was converted into a stronghold of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. The Crusaders are intolerant of all non-human races, regardless of alliance or affiliation. They believe that any and all outsiders are potential carriers of the undead plague - and must be destroyed.  ", d=29.550, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-ad5ec0ca", h="ad5ec0ca", t="No, I'm not, but lots of others are looking for love.  You should buy my love tokens, put on some cologne or perfume, and then pass them around!", d=9.520, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-adc7501c", h="adc7501c", t="The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.", d=8.360, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-b69e98a5", h="b69e98a5", t="If you put on cologne or perfume, then you'll see who is amorous.  Those are the ones who accept love tokens... and offer a gift in return.$B$BBut remember: to give someone a love token, you have to smell just right!  Men like the scent of perfume, while women prefer cologne.", d=18.280, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-b852ea17", h="b852ea17", t="Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm's fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade's existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council.  ", d=33.790, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-b8eefffb", h="b8eefffb", t="Shadowfang Keep is in southern Silverpine just north of Pyrewood Village.", d=5.600, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-b8ef9c65", h="b8ef9c65", t="The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.", d=5.000, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-c2bfa0cf", h="c2bfa0cf", t="Gnomeregan can be found in western Dun Morogh.", d=3.440, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-c80041d2", h="c80041d2", t="Welcome to my Inn, weary traveler. What can I do for you?", d=5.520, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-ca5fde90", h="ca5fde90", t="Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.", d=6.760, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-cfb4d237", h="cfb4d237", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook.  ", d=27.950, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-d352a290", h="d352a290", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook. ", d=27.470, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-e0b9e88a", h="e0b9e88a", t="Our ancient lands in the north east of the Eastern Kingdom. Named after Lordain himself, it was once a proud and powerful kingdom. Its history is rich and serves as many lessons to upstart nobles and kings. One of its defining moments was assisting in the foundation of the Alliance that we know today.    Unfortunately its history is also dark, and its current inhabitants defile its lands day by day. There is still much of significance in the ruins that now rest above the Undercity but it is folly to attempt that journey and expect to return still among the living.", d=38.460, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-e99614f5", h="e99614f5", t="The ruins of Zul'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.", d=6.800, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-f106f818", h="f106f818", t="Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara's most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres.  ", d=31.310, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-f2218c4a", h="f2218c4a", t="Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.", d=6.720, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-f88f28f5", h="f88f28f5", t="Ragefire Chasm can be found beneath the Shadow Cleft in the center of Orgrimmar.", d=5.880, v="human-female-official" },
		{ f="8931-f9fa0d11", h="f9fa0d11", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Cairne, Sylvanas and Thrall.", d=19.080, v="human-female-official" },
	},
	[8962] = {
		{ f="8962-0a5060df", h="0a5060df", t="I think my necklace fell in the lake.  My daddy got it for me, and he's gonna be mad now.", d=6.680, v="humanfemalekid-female" },
		{ f="8962-b692cafd", h="b692cafd", t="Thank you $g mister : miss; for finding my necklace!  You're the best!", d=4.080, v="humanfemalekid-female", g=true },
	},
	[8965] = {
		{ f="8965-29af2d0b", h="29af2d0b", t="Hello there $g mister : ma'am;... do you have a little time that you could help us out?  Please?", d=4.760, v="humanmalekid-male", g=true },
		{ f="8965-5a359b3f", h="5a359b3f", t="Hello there mister... do you have a little time that you could help us out?  Please?", d=5.600, v="humanmalekid-male" },
		{ f="8965-bb0bc8e7", h="bb0bc8e7", t="Hello there ma'am... do you have a little time that you could help us out?  Please?", d=5.760, v="humanmalekid-male" },
		{ f="8965-c5ffec2a", h="c5ffec2a", t="Thank you again for helping Hilary, $g mister : miss;!  When I grow up, I wanna be a hero just like you!", d=6.120, v="humanmalekid-male", g=true },
	},
	[9021] = {
		{ f="9021-25221b26", h="25221b26", t="She now resides at the side of Emperor Thaurissan. He has her under some sort of powerful thought altering spell... and here I sit, completely helpless. ", d=9.480, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9021-37e698bc", h="37e698bc", t="All is lost...", d=3.040, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9021-4e5b702e", h="4e5b702e", t="As we were making our way across the Burning Steppes, we were ambushed. It must have been a hundred of them... Dark Iron dwarves! They were shifting out of the walls, from the rocks in the Steppes; out of every crevice, nook, and cranny in sight. They swarmed us, overwhelming the guards and the few brave heroes that had agreed to assist us on this mission.$B$BOne thing was clear: This was a highly orchestrated ambush. It was as if they knew every move we would make before we made them...", d=27.350, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9021-5bbc6089", h="5bbc6089", t="How else could this have happened? Someone must have tipped the Dark Irons off.$B$B<Kharan shakes his fist at you.>$B$BSo help me, if I ever get out of here, I will spend the rest of my days finding the traitor.", d=9.680, v="dwarf-male", P={ { d=4.240 }, { d=2.240, n=true }, { d=5.680 } }, nP={ [1]={ [2]=3.320 } } },
		{ f="9021-5fb4ef5b", h="5fb4ef5b", t="Do I look stupid to you, $r? I may as well sign her death warrant myself! Why should I trust you? ", d=7.360, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9021-68d69b99", h="68d69b99", t="Get it over with you filthy $r.$B$B<Kharan lowers his head, exposing his stubby neck.>", d=2.960, v="dwarf-male", P={ { d=2.240 }, { d=3.560, n=true } }, nP={ [1]={ [2]=4.120 } } },
		{ f="9021-7aaf9afc", h="7aaf9afc", t="Where was I? Oh yes, so we were captured. My elite guardsmen were executed on the spot. They spared me and took the princess away by way of ram. I was taken to the detention halls of the Slag Pit and then transferred to this prison.$B$BI can only assume I am still alive because they wish to extract a ransom for my pitiful life. Or maybe out of cruelty, as a way to let me forever play back the events that transpired in my mind. Regret is the cruelest jailor of all, $r.", d=28.870, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9021-901741c2", h="901741c2", t="Then listen well, $r.$B$BSeveral months ago, the Magistrate of Lakeshire sent envoys to Ironforge, pleading with the King for assistance with the Blackrock incursions coming from Redridge and the Burning Steppes.$B$BPrincess Moira volunteered to help, against my pleadings. I was assigned twenty elite guardsmen to protect the Princess through the perilous journey from the Loch to Lakeshire.", d=21.470, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9021-ac64defa", h="ac64defa", t="<Kharan clears his throat.>$B$BWe made our way through the Searing Gorge tunnel and into the ravaged wasteland comprising the gorge. In retrospect, things were eerily quiet. The only dangers we ran across were the wildlife of the region: Creatures that my men easily dispatched.$B$BWe reached Blackrock Mountain with relative ease and made our way through the stonewrought construction without so much as a hiccup.", d=20.950, v="dwarf-male", P={ { d=2.040, n=true }, { d=21.750 } }, nP={ [1]={ [1]=2.200 } } },
		{ f="9021-b9c04921", h="b9c04921", t="<Kharan sighs.>$B$BI suppose... I suppose you are right.$B$BGor'shak told me that your Warchief has big plans. Plans that may change the way the Alliance and Horde interact. What do you know about this?", d=11.440, v="dwarf-male", P={ { d=2.320, n=true }, { d=11.280 } }, nP={ [1]={ [1]=3.040 } } },
	},
	[9022] = {
		{ f="9022-7c97d2ee", h="7c97d2ee", t="HELP!!!!", d=2.720, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
	},
	[9034] = {
		{ f="9034-21a6210b", h="21a6210b", t="The death of our flesh marked the birth of our spirit and our sacred task.", d=5.640, v="dwarf-female" },
	},
	[9035] = {
		{ f="9035-ac1102cc", h="ac1102cc", t="Our leader, Doom'rel, has ears for the challenge.", d=3.640, v="dwarf-male" },
	},
	[9036] = {
		{ f="9036-ac1102cc", h="ac1102cc", t="Our leader, Doom'rel, has ears for the challenge.", d=4.040, v="dwarf-male" },
	},
	[9037] = {
		{ f="9037-15ce3d8e", h="15ce3d8e", t="You have shown me your desire, and have payed with precious stone.  I will teach you...", d=5.800, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9037-4131c9b1", h="4131c9b1", t="Your will is strong, and your intent is clear.$B$BPerhaps you are worthy...", d=4.440, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9037-48580472", h="48580472", t="You wish to learn the old craft?  You wish to smelt dark iron?$B$BAppease me, $r.  Show me a sacrifice and I will consider it!", d=9.320, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9037-6812c5a7", h="6812c5a7", t="Interesting, interesting... I know of a druid that lives atop the hill above the Wailing Caverns, $n. She might be able to tell you more about this shard you have found.$B$BNow, I must get back to work!", d=11.760, v="dwarf-male" },
		{ f="9037-c162ca90", h="c162ca90", t="I am forever denied the touch of stone.  I will never again know the glory of shaped iron...", d=5.480, v="dwarf-male" },
	},
	[9038] = {
		{ f="9038-2b2ef6f0", h="2b2ef6f0", t="You may not pass.  You are not our kin, nor have you issued the challenge.", d=5.160, v="dwarf-female" },
	},
	[9039] = {
		{ f="9039-7c0276ec", h="7c0276ec", t="Our fate is the doom of all who face the Great Fire.", d=3.480, v="dwarf-male" },
	},
	[9040] = {
		{ f="9040-f666113e", h="f666113e", t="Our punishment is also our blessing.", d=3.120, v="dwarf-male" },
	},
	[9047] = {
		{ f="9047-56494cea", h="56494cea", t="Conspiracies abound, I say.  There are those who lack vision in understanding what I do, and would seek to keep me shackled to obscurity!$B$BDon't step in the dirt.", d=12.680, v="nightelf-male-standard" },
		{ f="9047-e8180e3e", h="e8180e3e", t="What am I doing?  Do you lack vision?  I am a dreamer, good $g sir : lady;, and I dream of a better future for us all.  Clearly, I am a visionary.$B$BThere are those, however, who seek to keep us mired in banality.  I told him that I was a dreamer, and Arch Druid Staghelm replied, \"Well, the world needs ditch diggers too.\"$B$BUntil such time as the shackles of banality are ripped from us, I will help the Cenarion Circle by shuffling these piles of dirt around.", d=32.030, v="nightelf-male-standard", g=true },
	},
	[9076] = {
		{ f="9076-6b8ae11d", h="6b8ae11d", t="Be advised, $g Jackson : Princess; - I am in no mood for any comment that you think is cute or funny.  I am here to make sure that the Arch Druid's research proceeds as planned, and my orders are to weed out all non-hackers who do not pack the gear to serve in my beloved Cenarion Circle.", d=16.667, v="tauren-male-warrior", g=true },
	},
	[9077] = {
		{ f="9077-29d5f228", h="29d5f228", t="And modest too... Perhaps it is your time, then, $n.$B$BAre you prepared to enter the fortress of the Blackrock orcs? To wreak havoc? To tear asunder the foundation of the mountain citadel?", d=15.880, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9077-d2ff3e9f", h="d2ff3e9f", t="I dream, $n... oh yes, I dream. In my dreams I die a thousand times in a thousand different ways. Some would call dreams such as mine nightmares. NOT I! In dreams I die in the thick of battle. For each single death of my own, ten thousand enemies of the Horde fall before me. It is glorious!", d=27.880, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9077-d4a9252d", h="d4a9252d", t="Truly, I envy you: To battle in the name of the Horde, at the forefront of conflict. Mine is a job of command.$B$BCertainly, in my youth, I lived out the dreams that make my old age bearable. I now revel in the glory of victory, the bitter taste of defeat - all through the soldiers I command. ", d=23.600, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9077-e57c6d3f", h="e57c6d3f", t="<Goretooth spits.>$B$BI am a warrior of the Horde, $n. It fills me with rage to know that our enemies sit in a fortress, less than a day's ride from Kargath, plotting against us.$B$BHow I long to break free from the bonds of duty and destroy them all in the name of the Warchief.$B$BAlas, we all have roles we must fulfill. ", d=27.670, v="orc-male-guard", P={ { d=1.920, n=true }, { d=28.950 } }, nP={ [1]={ [1]=2.080 } } },
		{ f="9077-f5b31b26", h="f5b31b26", t="I did not doubt you for even one second, $n.$B$BHere are your orders, $n. I know that you will not let me down. ", d=11.840, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9077-fbe9777a", h="fbe9777a", t="Aye, I could tell just by looking at you, $n. You remind me very much of myself as a young warrior of the Horde.$B$BYou will undoubtedly go far in life and even further in death.$B$B<Goretooth salutes.>", d=15.480, v="orc-male-guard", P={ { d=16.000 }, { d=1.560, n=true } }, nP={ [1]={ [2]=2.360 } } },
	},
	[9080] = {
		{ f="9080-cc6177cb", h="cc6177cb", t="I have no time for interruptions.", d=2.720, v="orc-male-shady" },
	},
	[9087] = {
		{ f="9087-e4fd33dd", h="e4fd33dd", t="Greetings, noble $c.  This humble servant of the Cenarion Circle wishes blessings and bounties be given unto you and yours.", d=10.920, v="tauren-female-shaman" },
	},
	[9099] = {
		{ f="9099-07b284ab", h="07b284ab", t="This cherry pie tastes so good, it could make a grown gnome cry.", d=2.944, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-2b8e5d50", h="2b8e5d50", t="Fresh cherry pie for sale, looks so good it will bring a tear to your eye.", d=3.234, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-738476a6", h="738476a6", t="Having a bad day? Try some cherry pie.", d=2.078, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-7cf55363", h="7cf55363", t="This pie is so good, would you like some?", d=2.262, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-a0631c3e", h="a0631c3e", t="Try some of this cherry pie, it will put a smile on your face, ten miles wide.", d=3.698, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-c91575ec", h="c91575ec", t="Nana always said there was no greater thing in the whole world than a warm, toasty slice of fresh, homemeade cherry pie.", d=5.052, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-e7c271a2", h="e7c271a2", t="I love pie.", d=0.932, v="gnome-male-young" },
		{ f="9099-e8063847", h="e8063847", t="Cherry pie is my favoritist food in all of Azeroth.", d=2.677, v="gnome-male-young" },
	},
	[9116] = {
		{ f="9116-252b454f", h="252b454f", t="The Emerald Circle strives to heal the wounded land of Felwood. Although the land is named for the very thing that has corrupted it, we hope that one day we will be able to eradicate the corruption from this land.", d=17.680, v="nightelf-female-priestess" },
	},
	[9117] = {
		{ f="9117-00b8b30a", h="00b8b30a", t="Sure thing, $n. Here's another for you.", d=2.260, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="9117-0b30557c", h="0b30557c", t="You probably weren't expecting to find me in this cave, were you?$B$BMy name's J.D., and I really can't tell you much about how I got here, but what I can tell you is that this cave is my home now!$B$BI spend my time studying the strange crystals that can be found all over the crater.", d=11.392, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="9117-0f1f26e4", h="0f1f26e4", t="The Eastern Pylon accepts blue, yellow, and green crystals.$B$BIt focuses on the energy that can be created using blue crystals as the main source of power. There are two possible effects: one provides bonus to spirit, and one that creates a damaging shield.$B$BCrystal Force requires blue and green crystals. This will provide you with an increase in spirit.$B$BCrystal Spire requires blue and yellow crystals. This will create a shield that does damage to attackers.  ", d=21.314, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="9117-21c5d425", h="21c5d425", t="The Northern Pylon accepts yellow, red, and green crystals.$B$BThe focus is the energy that can be created using yellow crystals as the main source of power. There are two possible effects: one that will produce damage, and one that will negate damage. $B$BCrystal Charge requires red and yellow crystals. This will produce a large explosion, stunning your enemies.$B$BCrystal Restore requires yellow and green crystals. This will provide you with a healing aura.", d=21.812, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="9117-a30f499b", h="a30f499b", t="The Western Pylon accepts red, green, and blue crystals.$B$BThe Pylon focuses on the energy that can be created using red crystals as the main source of power. There are two possible effects: one that increases your protection from damage, and one that weakens an enemy's defenses.$B$BCrystal Ward requires red and green crystals. This will provide you with an increase to armor.$B$BCrystal Yield requires blue and red crystals. This can lower the armor of a specific target.", d=21.874, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
		{ f="9117-f819026e", h="f819026e", t="Thanks to you, we can now unlock the secrets of the crystals and the mysterious pylons, $n. If you need more information at any time, please come back and visit me again!", d=7.864, v="gnome-female-nerdy" },
	},
	[9118] = {
		{ f="9118-672dca16", h="672dca16", t="Ugh... these pests keep me busy night and day! Haven't you seen them?$B$BI wish I could just jump down a pipe to get away from them...", d=8.280, v="dwarf-male-guard" },
	},
	[9270] = {
		{ f="9270-fa8306b3", h="fa8306b3", t="Hello stranger, and welcome to the untamed majesty of Un'Goro Crater!$B$BMy name is Williden Marshal.  My sister, our companions, and I make up Marshal Expeditions - scientists and explorers of Azeroth's wild and great unknown.$B$BWe've hit a bit of a rough patch here, and we're looking for some help if you have the time!", d=22.900, v="human-male-standard" },
	},
	[9271] = {
		{ f="9271-5bebf310", h="5bebf310", t="Oh, hello there!  I'm Hol'anyee, the chief scientist and biologist of Marshal Expeditions.  My brother and I, along with our companions, travel Azeroth exploring the wild and untamed majesty.  It is exciting... but, um... I think we got ourselves into a little too much excitement this time!", d=19.680, v="human-female-standard" },
	},
	[9272] = {
		{ f="9272-4f3ffa28", h="4f3ffa28", t="For the love of all that is holy and dear, please tell me that you've come to deliver us from this forsaken land.  Though I'm with Marshal Expeditions, I would give you the gold teeth from my mouth to climb inside your backpack and leave this place.", d=11.410, v="goblin-male-zany" },
		{ f="9272-e6c7606b", h="e6c7606b", t="Yeah yeah, I know Dadanga dislikes smoke.  From the smell of it though, seems like Dadanga also dislikes bathing.", d=6.441, v="goblin-male-zany" },
	},
	[9273] = {
		{ f="9273-b2860540", h="b2860540", t="Hello there, my name is Petra.  To my right is my kodo, Dadanga.  We're with Marshal Expeditions - been so for a few years now, ever since Dadanga was a babe.$B$BIf you have any lit torches or any open sources of flame, I'd like to ask you to keep them stashed if you could.  Dadanga dislikes smoke.", d=17.998, v="orc-female-warrior" },
		{ f="9273-d1166617", h="d1166617", t="Since we've begun our stay in the crater, Dadanga's taken a liking to the large bloodpetal sprouts that grow all over the place here.$B$BI'm sure she'd enjoy a snack, if you feel like bringing her some...", d=11.391, v="orc-female-warrior" },
	},
	[9298] = {
		{ f="9298-11d6024f", h="11d6024f", t="Hello! What brings you to Winterspring? These cold and vast lands may seem dismal, but this is a place of many secrets...", d=7.978, v="dwarf-female-maternal" },
	},
	[9299] = {
		{ f="9299-b7ee3e7a", h="b7ee3e7a", t="Very few seek me out... What may I do for you?", d=3.198, v="human-male" },
		{ f="9299-c5a462ca", h="c5a462ca", t="Please, leave an old spirit in peace.", d=3.202, v="human-male" },
	},
	[9356] = {
		{ f="9356-03ca5480", h="03ca5480", t="Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.   ", d=35.350, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-174473b0", h="174473b0", t="Recently, a night elf druid named Naralex discovered a network of underground caverns within the heart of the Barrens. Believing he could use the caverns' springs to restore lushness to the Barrens, the druid began siphoning the energies of the fabled Emerald Dream. His vision somehow became a nightmare, however, and soon the Wailing Caverns changed into a den of vicious, deadly predators. It is said that Naralex still resides somewhere inside the labyrinth, trapped beyond the edges of the Emerald Dream.  ", d=37.870, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-17e9d243", h="17e9d243", t="Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world's creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone.  ", d=43.380, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-19490f29", h="19490f29", t="Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar's spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ", d=44.190, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-19cbe7de", h="19cbe7de", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Bolvar, Magni, or Tyrande.", d=27.240, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-1a6e2552", h="1a6e2552", t="This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul'Farrak's walls. ", d=36.310, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-22aa3fe4", h="22aa3fe4", t="Razorfen Downs can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the east side of the road.", d=8.880, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-2e88eda5", h="2e88eda5", t="Frustrated by the Dalaran wizards' lack of progress against the undead during the Third War, the Archmage Arugal elected to summon the extra-dimensional worgen to bolster his side's diminishing ranks. The wolf-men slaughtered the Scourge, then quickly turned on the wizards themselves and laid siege to the keep of the noble, Baron Silverlaine. The fort quickly fell into shadow and ruin. Driven mad with guilt, Arugal adopted the worgen as his children and retreated to the newly dubbed 'Shadowfang Keep'.  ", d=39.940, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-3141b27b", h="3141b27b", t="Crafted from the same vines as Razorfen Kraul, Razorfen Downs is the traditional capital city of the quilboar race. The sprawling, thorn-ridden labyrinth houses a veritable army of loyal quilboar as well as their high priests - the Death's Head tribe. Recently, however, a looming shadow has fallen over the crude den. Agents of the undead Scourge - led by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer - have taken control over the quilboar race and turned the maze of thorns into a bastion of undead might.   ", d=42.710, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-330cd2db", h="330cd2db", t="The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves' holdings in the mountain's volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself.  ", d=35.950, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-33439fd8", h="33439fd8", t="Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal'ai's plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple's ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons. ", d=42.270, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-342c02c0", h="342c02c0", t="The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free.  ", d=31.950, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-4a0923b3", h="4a0923b3", t="Are you interested in exploring one of these dungeons?", d=5.080, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-4a6950fb", h="4a6950fb", t="The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.", d=4.560, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-4f48ef1f", h="4f48ef1f", t="Situated along the Zoram Strand of Ashenvale, Blackfathom Deeps was once a glorious temple dedicated to the night elves' moon-goddess Elune. However, the great Sundering shattered the temple - sinking it beneath the waves of the Veiled Sea. There it remained untouched - until, drawn by its ancient power - the naga and satyr emerged to plumb its secrets. Legends hold that the ancient beast, Aku'mai, has taken up residence within the temple's ruins.  ", d=42.870, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-581034a1", h="581034a1", t="The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ", d=44.390, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-5dc31760", h="5dc31760", t="During the War of the Ancients, the demigod Agamaggan came forth to battle the Burning Legion. The colossal boar was defeated, and over time in the areas where his blood fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted to life. The quilboar came to occupy these regions and hold them sacred. The heart of these massive thorn-colonies is the Razorfen. Razorfen Kraul was conquered by the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who some speculate has been negotiating with agents of the Scourge for some insidious purpose. ", d=43.430, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-5eccd4fa", h="5eccd4fa", t="The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.", d=7.040, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-5ff7a251", h="5ff7a251", t="Scarlet Monastery lies in the hills northeast of Tirisfal Glades.", d=5.640, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-66f64f6e", h="66f64f6e", t="Razorfen Kraul can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the west side of the road.", d=8.520, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-69040db4", h="69040db4", t="Love tokens are small messages of affection you can give to amorous town and city folk.  Such people will reward you with a gift of adoration.$B$BOr, if you are already adored by another, then at the least they'll give you a gift of friendship.", d=15.880, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-6a089d41", h="6a089d41", t="The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.", d=7.840, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-70185dce", h="70185dce", t="Uldaman can be found at the very northern end of the Badlands.", d=5.760, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-7161de72", h="7161de72", t="If we are to make these new lands ours then we must have places to rest our battle weary bodies. Lay your axe by the fire and share the stories of your mighty battles.", d=16.800, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-7b1bcef4", h="7b1bcef4", t="The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.", d=6.080, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-7de88db1", h="7de88db1", t="Located in Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan has been the gnomes' capital city for generations, though it was recently infested by mutant troggs. In a desperate attempt to retaliate, High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the emergency venting of the city's radioactive waste tanks. Though the troggs became irradiated, their siege continued unabated and the gnomes were forced to seek refuge in the dwarven city of Ironforge, where the High Tinker now enlists brave souls to help his people reclaim their beloved city.  ", d=39.910, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-864c5566", h="864c5566", t="The Wailing Caverns has its entrance at the Lushwater Oasis southwest of Crossroads in the Barrens.   ", d=8.520, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-95351c86", h="95351c86", t="Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat.  ", d=43.910, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-a9df0aa1", h="a9df0aa1", t="Blackfathom Deeps can be found at the north end of Zoram Strand along the coast of Ashenvale.", d=9.600, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-ab572ddf", h="ab572ddf", t="The monastery was once a center for learning and enlightenment. With the rise of the undead Scourge during the Third War, the peaceful Monastery was converted into a stronghold of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. The Crusaders are intolerant of all non-human races, regardless of alliance or affiliation. They believe that any and all outsiders are potential carriers of the undead plague - and must be destroyed.  ", d=32.030, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-ad5ec0ca", h="ad5ec0ca", t="No, I'm not, but lots of others are looking for love.  You should buy my love tokens, put on some cologne or perfume, and then pass them around!", d=12.200, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-adc7501c", h="adc7501c", t="The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.", d=9.120, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-b69e98a5", h="b69e98a5", t="If you put on cologne or perfume, then you'll see who is amorous.  Those are the ones who accept love tokens... and offer a gift in return.$B$BBut remember: to give someone a love token, you have to smell just right!  Men like the scent of perfume, while women prefer cologne.", d=25.800, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-b852ea17", h="b852ea17", t="Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm's fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade's existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council.  ", d=41.510, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-b8eefffb", h="b8eefffb", t="Shadowfang Keep is in southern Silverpine just north of Pyrewood Village.", d=6.680, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-b8ef9c65", h="b8ef9c65", t="The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.", d=5.720, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-c2bfa0cf", h="c2bfa0cf", t="Gnomeregan can be found in western Dun Morogh.", d=5.000, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-ca5fde90", h="ca5fde90", t="Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.", d=8.920, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-d352a290", h="d352a290", t="Once the greatest gold production center in the human lands, the Dead Mines are now inhabited by the Defias Brotherhood, who have turned the dark tunnels into their private sanctum. It is rumored that the thieves have conscripted the clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the mines - but what that may be is still uncertain. Rumor has it that the way into the Deadmines lies through the quiet, unassuming village of Moonbrook. ", d=34.670, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-e99614f5", h="e99614f5", t="The ruins of Zul'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.", d=8.680, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-f106f818", h="f106f818", t="Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara's most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres.  ", d=36.390, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-f2218c4a", h="f2218c4a", t="Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.", d=7.160, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-f88f28f5", h="f88f28f5", t="Ragefire Chasm can be found beneath the Shadow Cleft in the center of Orgrimmar.", d=8.080, v="orc-male-guard" },
		{ f="9356-f9fa0d11", h="f9fa0d11", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Cairne, Sylvanas and Thrall.", d=23.800, v="orc-male-guard" },
	},
	[9459] = {
		{ f="9459-04a76dd3", h="04a76dd3", t="Only a fool would dare disturb me in my lair.", d=2.840, v="narrator", n={ [1]=4.000 } },
		{ f="9459-2a55a1b0", h="2a55a1b0", t="<Cyrus's eyes glow brightly>$B$BDo I devour you whole or do I allow you to live?$B$BPerhaps you could still be of some use...$B$BChallenge my minion, $r. Survive and return proof of your victory to me.", d=13.120, v="narrator", n={ [1]=14.440 } },
	},
	[9465] = {
		{ f="9465-08830bac", h="08830bac", t="Through rigorous retraining I have had to break many students of all they had previously learned so that I might teach them anew.  The service I offer becomes increasingly difficult to perform each time it is done.  It is for that reason that it becomes increasingly expensive with each retraining.  Do you desire that I break you of the talents you have learned?", d=24.270, v="nightelf-male-official" },
		{ f="9465-8bdeec20", h="8bdeec20", t="Welcome, my $g brother : sister;.  If you are here to train, then I would be delighted to train you.$B$BWe are the preservers of the balance, now and forever, as Malfurion lies in the Dreaming.  Never forget this.", d=19.000, v="nightelf-male-official", g=true },
	},
	[9467] = {
		{ f="9467-54e3a7a1", h="54e3a7a1", t="Grumble, grumble...", d=1.107, v="human-male" },
	},
	[9500] = {
		{ f="9500-1f44f253", h="1f44f253", t="My master, Plugger Spazzring, is a good boss.  And he makes a lot of money.  His pockets are bursting!", d=6.668, v="human-female" },
		{ f="9500-45453757", h="45453757", t="Welcome to the Grim Guzzler!", d=2.042, v="human-female" },
		{ f="9500-53b460c0", h="53b460c0", t="Be sure to try our Dark Iron Ale.  I hear the dwarves around here can't get enough of it.", d=4.378, v="human-female" },
		{ f="9500-e91a5a1a", h="e91a5a1a", t="Thanks again, $n.  Rocknot and I are really hitting it off!", d=3.829, v="human-female" },
	},
	[9501] = {
		{ f="9501-03ca5480", h="03ca5480", t="Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.   ", d=35.630, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-174473b0", h="174473b0", t="Recently, a night elf druid named Naralex discovered a network of underground caverns within the heart of the Barrens. Believing he could use the caverns' springs to restore lushness to the Barrens, the druid began siphoning the energies of the fabled Emerald Dream. His vision somehow became a nightmare, however, and soon the Wailing Caverns changed into a den of vicious, deadly predators. It is said that Naralex still resides somewhere inside the labyrinth, trapped beyond the edges of the Emerald Dream.  ", d=41.070, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-17e9d243", h="17e9d243", t="Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world's creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone.  ", d=43.900, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-19490f29", h="19490f29", t="Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar's spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ", d=44.430, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-19cbe7de", h="19cbe7de", t="When you give love tokens to townsfolk, you'll receive different gifts in return.  Some of those you'll want to keep and use, but others can be bundled together and given to your favorite hero!  Visit Kwee Q. Peddlefeet to turn them in.$B$BKwee can be found near Bolvar, Magni, or Tyrande.", d=25.960, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-1a6e2552", h="1a6e2552", t="This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul'Farrak's walls. ", d=40.230, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-22aa3fe4", h="22aa3fe4", t="Razorfen Downs can be found on the very southern tip of the Barrens on the east side of the road.", d=8.920, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-2e88eda5", h="2e88eda5", t="Frustrated by the Dalaran wizards' lack of progress against the undead during the Third War, the Archmage Arugal elected to summon the extra-dimensional worgen to bolster his side's diminishing ranks. The wolf-men slaughtered the Scourge, then quickly turned on the wizards themselves and laid siege to the keep of the noble, Baron Silverlaine. The fort quickly fell into shadow and ruin. Driven mad with guilt, Arugal adopted the worgen as his children and retreated to the newly dubbed 'Shadowfang Keep'.  ", d=41.940, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-3141b27b", h="3141b27b", t="Crafted from the same vines as Razorfen Kraul, Razorfen Downs is the traditional capital city of the quilboar race. The sprawling, thorn-ridden labyrinth houses a veritable army of loyal quilboar as well as their high priests - the Death's Head tribe. Recently, however, a looming shadow has fallen over the crude den. Agents of the undead Scourge - led by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer - have taken control over the quilboar race and turned the maze of thorns into a bastion of undead might.   ", d=45.550, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-330cd2db", h="330cd2db", t="The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves' holdings in the mountain's volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself.  ", d=39.670, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-33439fd8", h="33439fd8", t="Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal'ai's plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple's ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons. ", d=42.110, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-342c02c0", h="342c02c0", t="The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free.  ", d=34.510, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-4a0923b3", h="4a0923b3", t="Are you interested in exploring one of these dungeons?", d=5.120, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-4a6950fb", h="4a6950fb", t="The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.", d=5.160, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-4f48ef1f", h="4f48ef1f", t="Situated along the Zoram Strand of Ashenvale, Blackfathom Deeps was once a glorious temple dedicated to the night elves' moon-goddess Elune. However, the great Sundering shattered the temple - sinking it beneath the waves of the Veiled Sea. There it remained untouched - until, drawn by its ancient power - the naga and satyr emerged to plumb its secrets. Legends hold that the ancient beast, Aku'mai, has taken up residence within the temple's ruins.  ", d=40.470, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-581034a1", h="581034a1", t="The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ", d=41.910, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-5dc31760", h="5dc31760", t="During the War of the Ancients, the demigod Agamaggan came forth to battle the Burning Legion. The colossal boar was defeated, and over time in the areas where his blood fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted to life. The quilboar came to occupy these regions and hold them sacred. The heart of these massive thorn-colonies is the Razorfen. Razorfen Kraul was conquered by the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who some speculate has been negotiating with agents of the Scourge for some insidious purpose. ", d=43.670, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-5eccd4fa", h="5eccd4fa", t="The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.", d=8.800, v="tauren-male-elder" },
		{ f="9501-5ff7a251", h="5ff7a251", t="Scarlet Monastery lies in the hills northeast of Tirisfal Glades.", d=5.560, v="tauren-male-elder" },
